  (7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It forces two friends to share one account', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'It deletes your account after two days', 'It slows down typing speed by half', 'b'),
  (7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'There is zero risk', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'c'),
  (7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'd'),
  (7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Allow everything without reading', 'Flashlights need your contacts to shine brighter', 'Give it microphone access too', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'd'),
  (7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Testing internet speed', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'Searching for ocean documentaries online', 'Cleaning computer fans', 'b'),
  (7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'c'),
  (7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'a'),
  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which shortcut CUTS (moves) selected text so you can paste it somewhere else?', 'Ctrl + C', 'Ctrl + X', 'Ctrl + K', 'Ctrl + M', 'b'),
  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'While watching a video on YouTube or VLC, pressing the Spacebar usually does what?', 'Pauses or plays the video', 'Deletes the video', 'Prints the screen', 'Shuts down the computer', 'a'),
  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which shortcut opens the PRINT box to print a page or save it as a PDF?', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + I', 'Ctrl + P', 'Ctrl + R', 'c'),
  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In Word or Google Docs, what does pressing Ctrl + B do to selected text?', 'Moves text to the bottom', 'Deletes the text', 'Turns the text Blue', 'Makes the text Bold (thicker)', 'd'),
  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a document editor, which shortcut makes selected text Italic (slanted)?', 'Ctrl + I', 'Ctrl + L', 'Ctrl + T', 'Ctrl + U', 'a'),
  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a document editor, which shortcut UNDERLINES the selected words?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + O', 'c'),
  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'What is the difference between the Backspace key and the Delete key while typing?', 'Backspace closes the program', 'Backspace erases to the left of the cursor; Delete erases to the right of the cursor', 'Both do the exact same thing', 'Delete only works on images', 'b'),
  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'If you want to quickly FIND a specific word on a long webpage or PDF, which shortcut do you press?', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + H', 'Ctrl + Q', 'Ctrl + G', 'a'),
