  (8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F2', 'F1', 'F8', 'F4', 'a'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which pocket-sized device plugs into a USB port to carry files between home and school?', 'Mouse Pad', 'USB Pendrive (Flash Drive)', 'Cooling Fan', 'UPS Battery', 'b'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'On a laptop, what is the flat touch-sensitive rectangle below the keyboard that works like a mouse?', 'Speaker Grill', 'Motherboard', 'Touchpad (Trackpad)', 'Hard Disk', 'c'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Pressing the RIGHT button on a computer mouse usually opens what?', 'Nothing at all', 'Computer shutdown screen', 'The DVD tray', 'A small shortcut/context menu with helpful options', 'd'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which classroom device shines your computer screen onto a large white wall or board so the whole class can watch?', 'Projector', 'Router', 'RAM stick', 'Scanner', 'a'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'On a smartphone or tablet, the screen both shows pictures AND senses your finger taps. What is it called?', 'Joystick', 'Touchscreen', 'Plotter', 'Barcode Reader', 'b'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What Does "Hardware" mean in simple everyday words?', 'Secret passwords', 'The physical parts of a computer that you can actually see and touch', 'Only paid mobile games', 'Websites on the internet', 'b'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'In Indian homes and school labs, a small box called a UPS is connected to desktop PCs. Why is it useful?', 'It makes games run faster', 'It prints color photos', 'It cleans computer viruses', 'It provides short battery backup during a power cut so you can save your work safely', 'd'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the opposite of a Printer — a device that turns a paper certificate or drawing into a digital image file on your PC?', 'Speaker', 'Scanner', 'Projector', 'Modem', 'b'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which single modern cable carries BOTH sharp high-definition video AND audio from a laptop to a TV or projector?', 'Power cord', 'HDMI cable', 'Earphone jack', 'Mouse wire', 'b'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'At a supermarket checkout or school library, which handheld device reads black-and-white striped labels instantly?', 'Joystick', 'Cooling Pad', 'Barcode Scanner', 'Microphone', 'c'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Why can a laptop keep running during a power cut even without an external UPS?', 'The keyboard generates power', 'Laptops run on Wi-Fi waves', 'Laptops have a built-in rechargeable battery inside', 'Laptops do not use electricity', 'c'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the tiny removable storage card used inside many cameras and Android phones called?', 'MicroSD (Memory) card', 'Credit card', 'Graphics card', 'SIM card', 'a'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the main job of the small spinning fan inside a laptop or desktop cabinet?', 'To make music louder', 'To blow dust onto the screen', 'To keep the processor and internal parts cool so the computer does not overheat', 'To boost Wi-Fi signal', 'c'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'In everyday phones and computers, what is the simple difference between RAM and Storage (SSD/ROM)?', 'RAM is only for printers', 'RAM stores photos forever; Storage deletes everything on restart', 'RAM holds active apps temporarily while working; Storage keeps your photos and files saved even when powered off', 'Both are names for the screen', 'c'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'If your computer opens 15 browser tabs and starts feeling sluggish when switching apps, having more of which part helps most?', 'A bigger mouse pad', 'A louder speaker', 'A longer power cable', 'RAM (working memory)', 'd'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Modern laptops use an SSD instead of an older spinning Hard Disk (HDD). What everyday benefit do you notice right away?', 'The laptop boots up and opens apps much faster, with no moving disk parts', 'The screen becomes wider', 'You never need to charge the battery', 'It prints paper automatically', 'a'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'VGA port', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)', 'CD-ROM slot', 'PS/2 round port', 'b'),
  (8, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Clipboard', 'Dashboard', 'Whiteboard', 'Motherboard', 'd'),
  (8, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Look at the file name "annual_day_photo.jpg". What kind of file is it?', 'A spreadsheet table', 'A computer virus', 'A picture / image file', 'A music song only', 'c'),
