  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'Look at an email address: `student@mapleskhatauli.com`. Which symbol always separates the username from the domain name?', '$ (Dollar)', '@ (At symbol)', '# (Hash)', '& (And)', 'b'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What is that square black-and-white patterned box on posters or ID cards that opens a link when scanned with a phone camera?', 'Emoji', 'CPU Chip', 'QR Code', 'SIM Card', 'c'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'Which of these is ALSO a popular web browser besides Google Chrome?', 'Mozilla Firefox / Microsoft Edge / Apple Safari', 'Windows Calculator', 'Adobe Photoshop', 'MS Excel', 'a'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'If you visited a helpful website yesterday and forgot its name, which browser list helps you find it again?', 'Browsing History (Ctrl + H)', 'Calculator History', 'Printer Queue', 'Bluetooth Devices', 'a'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What is the real difference between Google Chrome and Google Search?', 'Chrome is a search website; Google is a laptop brand', 'Chrome is the Browser app installed on your device; Google Search is a website used inside a browser to look up info', 'There is zero difference', 'Both are hardware parts', 'b'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'When you see `https://` and a padlock icon in the browser address bar before logging in, what does the "s" in `https` mean?', 'School-only website', 'Screen capture enabled', 'Secure — data between your browser and the website is encrypted so others on Wi-Fi cannot read your password', 'Slow connection', 'c'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'What does opening an "Incognito" or "Private" browser window ACTUALLY do on a shared computer?', 'It blocks all computer viruses automatically', 'It gives free unlimited mobile data', 'It makes you completely invisible to websites and your internet provider', 'It stops the browser from saving your browsing history, cookies, and login session on THAT computer after you close the window', 'd'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'If a webpage shows "404 — Page Not Found", what does that simply mean?', 'Your monitor is broken', '404 people are viewing the site', 'Your laptop battery is at 4%', 'The specific link or page was moved, deleted, or typed with a spelling mistake', 'd'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'When writing a polite email to a teacher or competition organizer, why should you always fill in the "Subject" line?', 'Subject is where you type your password', 'So the receiver immediately knows what your email is about before even opening it', 'Emails cannot be sent without 50 words in Subject', 'Subject hides your email address', 'b'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'If an expected registration confirmation email has not arrived in your Inbox, which email folder should you check next?', 'Downloads folder', 'Drafts folder', 'Spam / Junk folder', 'Recycle Bin on Desktop', 'c'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'Why do websites sometimes ask you to tick "I am not a robot" or pick traffic lights (CAPTCHA)?', 'To stop automated spam bots from creating fake accounts or flooding forms', 'To slow down your internet', 'To update your browser', 'To test your eyesight for driving', 'a'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'In Chrome or Edge, which shortcut opens your recent Downloads list directly inside the browser?', 'Ctrl + J', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + U', 'Alt + F4', 'a'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'What are website "Cookies" in everyday browsing?', 'Harmful hardware chips', 'Tiny text files saved by websites in your browser to remember things like your login status or dark-mode preference', 'Music playlists', 'Free gift vouchers', 'b'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'In Google Search, putting quotation marks around an exact phrase like `"Maples Academy Khatauli"` helps you find:', 'Pages that do NOT mention Maples Academy', 'Only videos', 'Pages containing that exact phrase with those words together in that order', 'Only images and no text', 'c'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'What is Google Drive or Microsoft OneDrive an example of?', 'A computer cooling pad', 'An offline painting program', 'A physical pendrive inside your pocket', 'Cloud storage — lets you save files online and open or share them from any phone or computer', 'd'),
  (8, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'When sharing a Google Drive project link with your teacher, why should you check whether access is set to "Restricted" vs "Anyone with the link can View"?', 'Restricted links delete the file', 'View access lets anyone delete your account', 'Links only work on Sundays', 'If left "Restricted", your teacher will see "Access Denied" when clicking your submitted link!', 'd'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'When you select a photo FROM your computer and post/submit it TO an online portal, is that called Downloading or Uploading?', 'Downloading', 'Formatting', 'Rebooting', 'Uploading', 'd'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Look at the curved fan-shaped icon with 3 or 4 arcs in the corner of your phone or laptop screen. What does it show?', 'Screen brightness', 'Wi-Fi connection and signal strength', 'Speaker volume level', 'CPU temperature', 'b'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Which of these tasks works completely OFFLINE even when you have zero internet connection?', 'Searching on Google', 'Streaming a live YouTube video', 'Using the built-in Calculator or typing in Notepad', 'Sending an email', 'c'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Why do home and school Wi-Fi networks have a password?', 'So strangers outside cannot use your internet or access devices on your network', 'To make the router light turn blue', 'To charge phones faster', 'Because routers cannot turn on without a 20-letter name', 'a'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'When a YouTube video pauses with a spinning circle in the middle because the internet is slow, what is that called?', 'Buffering', 'Scanning', 'Printing', 'Zipping', 'a'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Roughly how far does normal Bluetooth (like wireless earbuds connected to your phone) usually reach clearly?', 'Across the entire state (500 km)', 'A short room-size distance (around 10 meters / 30 feet)', 'Only 1 millimeter', 'Around the whole planet', 'b'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Your laptop says "Connected to Wi-Fi, No Internet." What does this message actually mean?', 'Your screen is damaged', 'You forgot your laptop password', 'Your laptop is connected to the Wi-Fi router in the room, but the router’s outside internet line is down', 'Your laptop Wi-Fi card is broken', 'c'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Why are desktop computers in an exam lab often connected by Ethernet (LAN) cables instead of Wi-Fi?', 'Wi-Fi only works on phones', 'LAN cables also power the monitor without electricity', 'Desktop PCs can never use Wi-Fi', 'A wired Ethernet cable gives steadier, interference-free internet for 30+ PCs at the same time', 'd'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Internet plan speeds from providers like JioFiber, Airtel, or BSNL are commonly advertised in "100 Mbps". What does Mbps measure?', 'How many months the plan lasts', 'How many devices are allowed', 'How far the Wi-Fi reaches in meters', 'Megabits per second — how fast data transfers over your internet connection', 'd'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Companies like BSNL, Airtel, Jio, or local fiber broadband providers that connect homes/schools to the internet are called:', 'Search Engines', 'ISPs (Internet Service Providers)', 'Web Browsers', 'Operating Systems', 'b'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Why does Wi-Fi signal become weaker when you walk three rooms away behind thick concrete walls?', 'Gravity pulls Wi-Fi down', 'Wi-Fi needs sunlight to travel', 'Thick walls and distance absorb and weaken wireless radio waves from the router', 'The phone screen gets smaller', 'c'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What is a "Local Area Network (LAN)" in simple everyday words?', 'Computers, laptops, and printers connected together inside one building, home, or school campus', 'A type of USB pendrive', 'An antivirus program', 'Satellites orbiting Mars', 'a'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'If ONE Wi-Fi printer is connected to the school office Wi-Fi router, how many computers on that same Wi-Fi can print to it?', 'All authorized computers/phones on that same Wi-Fi network can share and print to it wirelessly', 'Zero — Wi-Fi printers cannot print', 'Only a computer plugged into it with an HDMI cable', 'Only phones with no SIM card', 'a'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'When you mirror your phone or laptop screen wirelessly onto a classroom Smart TV without any cable, what is that feature called?', 'Disk Formatting', 'Screen Casting / Screen Mirroring', 'Incognito Browsing', 'Zipping', 'b'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Every device connected to a network gets an identifying number address (like a house number for delivering data packets). What is it called?', 'Roll Number', 'Font Size', 'IP Address', 'PIN Code', 'c'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'You are using a 1.5 GB/day mobile data pack via Hotspot. Watching 2 hours of video at `4K / 2160p` vs `480p` will do what?', 'Resolution only affects audio volume', 'Both use zero mobile data', '`4K` uses less data than `480p`', '`4K` uses many times more mobile data and can finish your 1.5 GB pack very quickly!', 'd'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It makes the screen brighter', 'It doubles keyboard speed', 'It uninstalls browsers', 'It pauses huge background Windows updates so your friend’s mobile data does not drain suddenly', 'd'),
  (8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', '`2.4G` works only at 2:40 PM', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', '`5G` Wi-Fi requires a 5G SIM card inside the router', 'There is no difference at all', 'b'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why shouldn’t you eat sticky snacks or keep an open cup of water right over a computer keyboard?', 'Water changes the wallpaper', 'Crumbs and spilled liquid can permanently short-circuit and ruin the keyboard or laptop', 'Food slows down Google Search', 'Snacks reduce Wi-Fi bars', 'b'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If a pop-up flashes on screen: "🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! You won a free iPhone! Click here & enter your details!", what is it almost certainly?', 'A Windows system update', 'A real gift from your browser', 'A scam / phishing trap trying to steal personal details or install malware — close it immediately!', 'An official CBSE scholarship', 'c'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What is "Netiquette"?', 'Good manners, kindness, and respectful behavior when communicating on the internet', 'A type of mosquito net', 'An offline calculator game', 'A brand of Ethernet cable', 'a'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Should you share your home address, school timetable, and phone number publicly with unknown strangers in online game chats?', 'No — keep personal details private to stay safe online', 'Yes, if they offer free game coins', 'Yes, if they have a cool profile picture', 'Yes, on every public comment section', 'a'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Crop out their name and claim it as yours', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself', 'Never use books or references', 'Forbid anyone else from seeing the source', 'b'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Open 20 tabs at brightness 20%', 'Blink only 20 times a day', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'Sit 20 millimeters from the screen for 20 hours', 'c'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'UPI PIN is just your roll number', 'Yes, scanning any QR code automatically credits money after PIN', 'Yes, you must enter UPI PIN to receive gifts', 'NEVER! A UPI PIN is ONLY entered when money is GOING OUT from your account — asking you to enter PIN to "receive" money is a scam!', 'd'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It forces two friends to share one account', 'It slows down typing speed by half', 'It deletes your account after two days', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'd'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'There is zero risk', 'b'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'c'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Flashlights need your contacts to shine brighter', 'Give it microphone access too', 'Allow everything without reading', 'a'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'Searching for ocean documentaries online', 'Testing internet speed', 'Cleaning computer fans', 'a'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'b'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'c'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Share it with the café owner', 'Write your password on a sticky note on the monitor', 'Click "Save" so you never have to type again', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'd'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Sending 80 stickers in a row at midnight', 'Starting personal arguments in front of 60 people', 'Forwarding unverified rumors', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'd'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To slow down your internet', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To erase your photos', 'b'),
  (8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Change their account password', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'c'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a document editor, which shortcut makes selected text Italic (slanted)?', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + L', 'Ctrl + T', 'Ctrl + I', 'd'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a document editor, which shortcut UNDERLINES the selected words?', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + O', 'b'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'What is the difference between the Backspace key and the Delete key while typing?', 'Backspace erases to the left of the cursor; Delete erases to the right of the cursor', 'Both do the exact same thing', 'Backspace closes the program', 'Delete only works on images', 'a'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'If you want to quickly FIND a specific word on a long webpage or PDF, which shortcut do you press?', 'Ctrl + H', 'Ctrl + Q', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + G', 'c'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which key at the top-left of the keyboard is commonly pressed to cancel a pop-up or exit full-screen video?', 'Num Lock', 'Insert', 'Esc (Escape)', 'Tab', 'c'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which function key is the classic shortcut to REFRESH or reload a webpage in a browser?', 'F2', 'F5', 'F12', 'F1', 'b'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'If you pressed Ctrl + Z (Undo) by mistake and want your change back, which shortcut performs REDO?', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + Y', 'Ctrl + R', 'Ctrl + E', 'b'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which keyboard shortcut lets you quickly switch between open apps/windows on Windows?', 'Ctrl + P', 'Alt + Tab', 'Ctrl + C', 'Shift + Enter', 'b'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Alt', 'Shift', 'Tab', 'Ctrl', 'b'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + D', 'a'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Opens a new browser tab', 'Closes the browser', 'Turns off Wi-Fi', 'Translates the page', 'a'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Turns the screen white', 'Saves all bookmarks', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens Microsoft Word', 'c'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'Pause/Break', 'Page Down', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Scroll Lock', 'c'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F2', 'F4', 'F8', 'F1', 'a'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Increases speaker volume', 'Opens four new folders', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Turns on Bluetooth', 'c'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Opens calculator', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'Adds a new user account', 'Increases internet speed', 'b'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Deletes the webpage', 'Mutes computer sound', 'Closes all tabs', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'd'),
  (9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Submits the form immediately', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Erases what you typed', 'Closes the browser tab', 'b'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'On a smartphone or tablet, the screen both shows pictures AND senses your finger taps. What is it called?', 'Touchscreen', 'Plotter', 'Joystick', 'Barcode Reader', 'a'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What Does "Hardware" mean in simple everyday words?', 'The physical parts of a computer that you can actually see and touch', 'Only paid mobile games', 'Secret passwords', 'Websites on the internet', 'a'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'In Indian homes and school labs, a small box called a UPS is connected to desktop PCs. Why is it useful?', 'It prints color photos', 'It cleans computer viruses', 'It makes games run faster', 'It provides short battery backup during a power cut so you can save your work safely', 'd'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What is the opposite of a Printer — a device that turns a paper certificate or drawing into a digital image file on your PC?', 'Modem', 'Projector', 'Scanner', 'Speaker', 'c'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which single modern cable carries BOTH sharp high-definition video AND audio from a laptop to a TV or projector?', 'Power cord', 'Mouse wire', 'Earphone jack', 'HDMI cable', 'd'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'At a supermarket checkout or school library, which handheld device reads black-and-white striped labels instantly?', 'Joystick', 'Barcode Scanner', 'Microphone', 'Cooling Pad', 'b'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Why can a laptop keep running during a power cut even without an external UPS?', 'The keyboard generates power', 'Laptops have a built-in rechargeable battery inside', 'Laptops do not use electricity', 'Laptops run on Wi-Fi waves', 'b'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the tiny removable storage card used inside many cameras and Android phones called?', 'SIM card', 'Credit card', 'Graphics card', 'MicroSD (Memory) card', 'd'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the main job of the small spinning fan inside a laptop or desktop cabinet?', 'To blow dust onto the screen', 'To keep the processor and internal parts cool so the computer does not overheat', 'To make music louder', 'To boost Wi-Fi signal', 'b'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'In everyday phones and computers, what is the simple difference between RAM and Storage (SSD/ROM)?', 'RAM stores photos forever; Storage deletes everything on restart', 'RAM holds active apps temporarily while working; Storage keeps your photos and files saved even when powered off', 'RAM is only for printers', 'Both are names for the screen', 'b'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'If your computer opens 15 browser tabs and starts feeling sluggish when switching apps, having more of which part helps most?', 'A louder speaker', 'A longer power cable', 'A bigger mouse pad', 'RAM (working memory)', 'd'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Modern laptops use an SSD instead of an older spinning Hard Disk (HDD). What everyday benefit do you notice right away?', 'It prints paper automatically', 'You never need to charge the battery', 'The screen becomes wider', 'The laptop boots up and opens apps much faster, with no moving disk parts', 'd'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'VGA port', 'PS/2 round port', 'CD-ROM slot', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)', 'd'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Clipboard', 'Whiteboard', 'Motherboard', 'Dashboard', 'c'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'If a wireless mouse stops moving the cursor on screen, what is the FIRST simple hardware thing you should check?', 'Delete your files', 'Check if its battery is low or its tiny power switch underneath is turned OFF', 'Reinstall Windows immediately', 'Buy a new monitor', 'b'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'A pen-like tool used by digital artists and students to write or draw neatly on a tablet screen is called a:', 'Stylus', 'Router antenna', 'Thumb drive', 'Laser printer', 'a'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Which storage capacity is LARGER when comparing a pendrive or laptop storage?', '1 Terabyte (1 TB)', '1 Gigabyte (1 GB)', '1 Megabyte (1 MB)', '1 Kilobyte (1 KB)', 'a'),
  (9, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Roughly how many Gigabytes (GB) make 1 Terabyte (TB) on a hard drive?', 'About 1,000 GB (1,024 GB)', 'About 10 GB', 'About 2 GB', 'About 50 GB', 'a'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Which popular design app/website lets students easily create posters, certificates, and invitations using ready templates?', 'Command Prompt', 'Canva', 'Device Manager', 'Disk Cleanup', 'b'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What does "Software" mean in simple everyday language?', 'The plastic keyboard keys', 'The power socket on the wall', 'Soft cloth used to clean a monitor', 'The apps, programs, and operating system that run inside a computer or phone', 'd'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Which of the following is an Operating System (the core system software that runs a PC or phone)?', 'WhatsApp', 'Canva', 'YouTube', 'Windows 11 / Android', 'd'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Why do schools send circulars and admit cards as a ".pdf" file instead of an editable Word file?', 'PDFs only open at night', 'PDFs automatically translate into 50 languages', 'PDFs do not take even 1 byte of space', 'PDFs keep the exact layout, fonts, and alignment looking identical on every phone and computer', 'd'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Which application is best suited for keeping an attendance list, marks table, or club budget with automatic totals?', 'Sound Recorder', 'Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets', 'MS Paint', 'Photos viewer', 'b'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What is the difference between "Copy & Paste" and "Cut & Paste" on a file?', 'There is no difference', 'Cut deletes the file permanently', 'Copy leaves the original file in place and makes a duplicate; Cut moves the file to the new folder', 'Copy works only on photos', 'c'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What is a ".zip" file commonly used for when sharing a project?', 'Bundling many files/folders together into one smaller compressed file for easy sending', 'Charging laptop battery faster', 'Changing desktop wallpaper', 'Making music play faster', 'a'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'In Word or Google Docs, what is the difference between "Save" and "Save As"?', '"Save" updates the current file; "Save As" lets you save a separate copy with a new name or location', '"Save As" deletes the old file', '"Save" only works offline', 'Both print the document on paper', 'a'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'Which long bar at the bottom of a Windows screen shows the Start button, pinned apps, and clock?', 'Scroll bar', 'Taskbar', 'Bookmark bar', 'Formula bar', 'b'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'Why do many students turn on "Dark Mode" in apps when reading or working in the evening?', 'It doubles storage space', 'It prints pages in black paper', 'It uses a dark background that feels gentler on the eyes in low light', 'It makes Wi-Fi twice as fast', 'c'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'If you want to jot down a quick plain-text note with zero heavy formatting, which lightweight built-in Windows app opens instantly?', 'Media Player', 'Disk Defragmenter', 'Device Manager', 'Notepad', 'd'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'When saving an image with a transparent background (such as a school logo), which image format supports transparency cleanly?', '.mp3', '.txt', '.exe', '.png', 'd'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'On Windows, files ending in ".exe" (or ".apk" on Android) are what kind of files?', 'Family vacation photos', 'Application installer / executable program files (only run from trusted official sources!)', 'Plain text essays', 'Spreadsheet charts', 'b'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'Before editing an important project presentation, why is naming files clearly like "Science_Poster_v2_Final.pptx" better than "asdf123.pptx"?', 'It changes slide colors automatically', 'Computers refuse to save short names', 'Clear file names let you and your teammates find the right version in seconds without confusion', 'Long names increase RAM', 'c'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'What does the "Spell Check" wavy red underline in Word or Google Docs indicate?', 'A word that may have a spelling typo so you can review and fix it', 'That the sentence will be deleted automatically', 'That the font is bold', 'That the computer has a virus', 'a'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'If a single app stops responding ("Not Responding") on Windows, how can you close JUST that stuck app without unplugging the whole PC?', 'Open Task Manager, select the frozen app, and click "End Task"', 'Pull the electric plug from the wall', 'Format the hard drive', 'Tap the monitor glass', 'a'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'What is "Open-Source Software" (such as Linux, VLC, Blender, or LibreOffice)?', 'Software that leaves your computer unlocked to strangers', 'Software whose source code is openly shared so anyone can use, study, and improve it legally', 'Broken trial software', 'Software that works only for 1 hour', 'b'),
  (9, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'When you install a new PDF app and Windows asks which "Default App" should open .pdf files, what does that setting control?', 'How fast the internet runs', 'Whether printing is allowed', 'Which program opens automatically whenever you double-click any .pdf file', 'Which user owns the computer', 'c'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'Which of these is ALSO a popular web browser besides Google Chrome?', 'Windows Calculator', 'Adobe Photoshop', 'Mozilla Firefox / Microsoft Edge / Apple Safari', 'MS Excel', 'c'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'If you visited a helpful website yesterday and forgot its name, which browser list helps you find it again?', 'Bluetooth Devices', 'Printer Queue', 'Calculator History', 'Browsing History (Ctrl + H)', 'd'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What is the real difference between Google Chrome and Google Search?', 'Chrome is a search website; Google is a laptop brand', 'Both are hardware parts', 'There is zero difference', 'Chrome is the Browser app installed on your device; Google Search is a website used inside a browser to look up info', 'd'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'When you see `https://` and a padlock icon in the browser address bar before logging in, what does the "s" in `https` mean?', 'School-only website', 'Secure — data between your browser and the website is encrypted so others on Wi-Fi cannot read your password', 'Slow connection', 'Screen capture enabled', 'b'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What does opening an "Incognito" or "Private" browser window ACTUALLY do on a shared computer?', 'It blocks all computer viruses automatically', 'It makes you completely invisible to websites and your internet provider', 'It stops the browser from saving your browsing history, cookies, and login session on THAT computer after you close the window', 'It gives free unlimited mobile data', 'c'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'If a webpage shows "404 — Page Not Found", what does that simply mean?', 'The specific link or page was moved, deleted, or typed with a spelling mistake', '404 people are viewing the site', 'Your laptop battery is at 4%', 'Your monitor is broken', 'a'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'When writing a polite email to a teacher or competition organizer, why should you always fill in the "Subject" line?', 'So the receiver immediately knows what your email is about before even opening it', 'Emails cannot be sent without 50 words in Subject', 'Subject is where you type your password', 'Subject hides your email address', 'a'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'If an expected registration confirmation email has not arrived in your Inbox, which email folder should you check next?', 'Drafts folder', 'Spam / Junk folder', 'Downloads folder', 'Recycle Bin on Desktop', 'b'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'Why do websites sometimes ask you to tick "I am not a robot" or pick traffic lights (CAPTCHA)?', 'To slow down your internet', 'To update your browser', 'To stop automated spam bots from creating fake accounts or flooding forms', 'To test your eyesight for driving', 'c'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'In Chrome or Edge, which shortcut opens your recent Downloads list directly inside the browser?', 'Alt + F4', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + J', 'd'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'What are website "Cookies" in everyday browsing?', 'Harmful hardware chips', 'Free gift vouchers', 'Music playlists', 'Tiny text files saved by websites in your browser to remember things like your login status or dark-mode preference', 'd'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'In Google Search, putting quotation marks around an exact phrase like `"Maples Academy Khatauli"` helps you find:', 'Pages that do NOT mention Maples Academy', 'Pages containing that exact phrase with those words together in that order', 'Only images and no text', 'Only videos', 'b'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'What is Google Drive or Microsoft OneDrive an example of?', 'A computer cooling pad', 'A physical pendrive inside your pocket', 'Cloud storage — lets you save files online and open or share them from any phone or computer', 'An offline painting program', 'c'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'When sharing a Google Drive project link with your teacher, why should you check whether access is set to "Restricted" vs "Anyone with the link can View"?', 'If left "Restricted", your teacher will see "Access Denied" when clicking your submitted link!', 'View access lets anyone delete your account', 'Links only work on Sundays', 'Restricted links delete the file', 'a'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'On a noisy browser tab playing unexpected music, what does the tiny speaker icon on that tab let you see or do?', 'Spot immediately which tab is playing sound and even mute that tab', 'Record your microphone', 'Bookmark the website', 'Print the tab', 'a'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'What does an email ending in `.edu.in`, `.ac.in`, or `.gov.in` in India tell you about the website/sender?', 'Anyone can buy it anonymously for ₹10 without verification', 'It belongs to a verified Indian educational institution (`.edu.in`/`.ac.in`) or government body (`.gov.in`)', 'It only works without internet', 'It is a gaming server', 'b'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'If you start writing an email in Gmail and close the tab before clicking Send, where is your unfinished message saved automatically?', 'Sent', 'Starred', 'Drafts', 'Spam', 'c'),
  (9, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'What is a "Browser Extension" (or Add-on)?', 'A Wi-Fi booster antenna', 'A second monitor screen', 'An extra long charging cable', 'A small optional helper tool added inside your browser (which you should install ONLY from trusted creators)', 'd'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'When a YouTube video pauses with a spinning circle in the middle because the internet is slow, what is that called?', 'Zipping', 'Printing', 'Scanning', 'Buffering', 'd'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Roughly how far does normal Bluetooth (like wireless earbuds connected to your phone) usually reach clearly?', 'Across the entire state (500 km)', 'Around the whole planet', 'Only 1 millimeter', 'A short room-size distance (around 10 meters / 30 feet)', 'd'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Your laptop says "Connected to Wi-Fi, No Internet." What does this message actually mean?', 'Your screen is damaged', 'Your laptop is connected to the Wi-Fi router in the room, but the router’s outside internet line is down', 'Your laptop Wi-Fi card is broken', 'You forgot your laptop password', 'b'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Why are desktop computers in an exam lab often connected by Ethernet (LAN) cables instead of Wi-Fi?', 'Wi-Fi only works on phones', 'Desktop PCs can never use Wi-Fi', 'A wired Ethernet cable gives steadier, interference-free internet for 30+ PCs at the same time', 'LAN cables also power the monitor without electricity', 'c'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Internet plan speeds from providers like JioFiber, Airtel, or BSNL are commonly advertised in "100 Mbps". What does Mbps measure?', 'Megabits per second — how fast data transfers over your internet connection', 'How many devices are allowed', 'How far the Wi-Fi reaches in meters', 'How many months the plan lasts', 'a'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Companies like BSNL, Airtel, Jio, or local fiber broadband providers that connect homes/schools to the internet are called:', 'ISPs (Internet Service Providers)', 'Web Browsers', 'Search Engines', 'Operating Systems', 'a'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Why does Wi-Fi signal become weaker when you walk three rooms away behind thick concrete walls?', 'Wi-Fi needs sunlight to travel', 'Thick walls and distance absorb and weaken wireless radio waves from the router', 'Gravity pulls Wi-Fi down', 'The phone screen gets smaller', 'b'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What is a "Local Area Network (LAN)" in simple everyday words?', 'A type of USB pendrive', 'An antivirus program', 'Computers, laptops, and printers connected together inside one building, home, or school campus', 'Satellites orbiting Mars', 'c'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'If ONE Wi-Fi printer is connected to the school office Wi-Fi router, how many computers on that same Wi-Fi can print to it?', 'Only phones with no SIM card', 'Only a computer plugged into it with an HDMI cable', 'Zero — Wi-Fi printers cannot print', 'All authorized computers/phones on that same Wi-Fi network can share and print to it wirelessly', 'd'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'When you mirror your phone or laptop screen wirelessly onto a classroom Smart TV without any cable, what is that feature called?', 'Disk Formatting', 'Zipping', 'Incognito Browsing', 'Screen Casting / Screen Mirroring', 'd'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Every device connected to a network gets an identifying number address (like a house number for delivering data packets). What is it called?', 'Roll Number', 'IP Address', 'PIN Code', 'Font Size', 'b'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'You are using a 1.5 GB/day mobile data pack via Hotspot. Watching 2 hours of video at `4K / 2160p` vs `480p` will do what?', 'Resolution only affects audio volume', '`4K` uses less data than `480p`', '`4K` uses many times more mobile data and can finish your 1.5 GB pack very quickly!', 'Both use zero mobile data', 'c'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It pauses huge background Windows updates so your friend’s mobile data does not drain suddenly', 'It doubles keyboard speed', 'It uninstalls browsers', 'It makes the screen brighter', 'a'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', '`5G` Wi-Fi requires a 5G SIM card inside the router', '`2.4G` works only at 2:40 PM', 'There is no difference at all', 'a'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What is "Quick Share / Nearby Share / AirDrop" on modern phones and laptops used for?', 'Charging another phone from 10 meters away', 'Sending photos or project files fast between two nearby devices wirelessly without wasting internet data', 'Scanning paper books', 'Deleting duplicate contacts', 'b'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Why should you avoid logging into banking or sensitive accounts on an open, password-free public Wi-Fi at a railway station or café?', 'Public Wi-Fi breaks your phone camera', 'Public Wi-Fi deletes SIM contacts', 'Unsecured open Wi-Fi networks make it easier for attackers nearby to snoop on traffic or set up fake twin hotspots', 'Public Wi-Fi drains battery 10x faster', 'c'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'In online video calls or multiplayer games, what does "High Ping / High Latency" (e.g., 450 ms instead of 25 ms) feel like?', 'More storage space', 'Higher screen brightness', 'Extra crisp sound quality', 'A noticeable delay or lag between clicking/speaking and getting a response back', 'd'),
  (9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What brings ultrahigh-speed broadband into modern schools and homes using hair-thin strands of glass carrying pulses of light?', 'Aux Audio Cable', 'VGA Monitor Cable', 'Printer Ribbon', 'Fiber-Optic Cable', 'd'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Crop out their name and claim it as yours', 'Forbid anyone else from seeing the source', 'Never use books or references', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself', 'd'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Open 20 tabs at brightness 20%', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'Sit 20 millimeters from the screen for 20 hours', 'Blink only 20 times a day', 'b'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'UPI PIN is just your roll number', 'Yes, you must enter UPI PIN to receive gifts', 'NEVER! A UPI PIN is ONLY entered when money is GOING OUT from your account — asking you to enter PIN to "receive" money is a scam!', 'Yes, scanning any QR code automatically credits money after PIN', 'c'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'It slows down typing speed by half', 'It deletes your account after two days', 'It forces two friends to share one account', 'a'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'There is zero risk', 'a'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'b'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Flashlights need your contacts to shine brighter', 'Give it microphone access too', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Allow everything without reading', 'c'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Cleaning computer fans', 'Testing internet speed', 'Searching for ocean documentaries online', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'd'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'd'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'b'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Share it with the café owner', 'Click "Save" so you never have to type again', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'Write your password on a sticky note on the monitor', 'c'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Starting personal arguments in front of 60 people', 'Forwarding unverified rumors', 'Sending 80 stickers in a row at midnight', 'a'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To slow down your internet', 'To erase your photos', 'a'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Change their account password', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'b'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Never read what you submit', 'Turn off spell check', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Assume computers can never be wrong', 'c'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'Batteries charge only when silent', 'Night Wi-Fi costs double', 'Phones stop working after 10 PM', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'd'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Send them your phone number to argue back', 'Click every link they sent', 'Keep it secret and worry alone', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'd'),
  (9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Using open-source software legally', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'Saving a backup copy on a pendrive', 'Checking spelling in Word', 'b'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which key at the top-left of the keyboard is commonly pressed to cancel a pop-up or exit full-screen video?', 'Num Lock', 'Esc (Escape)', 'Tab', 'Insert', 'b'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which function key is the classic shortcut to REFRESH or reload a webpage in a browser?', 'F1', 'F5', 'F12', 'F2', 'b'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'If you pressed Ctrl + Z (Undo) by mistake and want your change back, which shortcut performs REDO?', 'Ctrl + Y', 'Ctrl + R', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + E', 'a'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which keyboard shortcut lets you quickly switch between open apps/windows on Windows?', 'Alt + Tab', 'Ctrl + C', 'Ctrl + P', 'Shift + Enter', 'a'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Shift', 'Tab', 'Alt', 'Ctrl', 'a'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + N', 'd'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Opens a new browser tab', 'Translates the page', 'Turns off Wi-Fi', 'Closes the browser', 'a'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Turns the screen white', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens Microsoft Word', 'Saves all bookmarks', 'b'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'Pause/Break', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Scroll Lock', 'Page Down', 'b'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F1', 'F4', 'F8', 'F2', 'd'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Opens four new folders', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Increases speaker volume', 'Turns on Bluetooth', 'b'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'Adds a new user account', 'Opens calculator', 'Increases internet speed', 'a'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Mutes computer sound', 'Closes all tabs', 'Deletes the webpage', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'd'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Closes the browser tab', 'Erases what you typed', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Submits the form immediately', 'c'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'If you step away from a computer for a minute, which Windows shortcut immediately LOCKS your screen?', 'Windows Key + O', 'Ctrl + L', 'Alt + L', 'Windows Key + L', 'd'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'Which Windows shortcut minimizes all open windows at once so you can see the Desktop?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Windows Key + D', 'Windows Key + P', 'Alt + D', 'b'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'You accidentally closed an important tab in Chrome/Edge! Which lifesaver shortcut reopens the last closed tab?', 'Alt + Home', 'Ctrl + Alt + Z', 'Ctrl + Shift + T', 'Shift + F5', 'c'),
  (10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'What happens when you delete a file using Shift + Delete instead of just pressing Delete?', 'It copies the file twice', 'It moves the file to Desktop', 'Nothing happens', 'It permanently deletes the file without sending it to the Recycle Bin', 'd'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which single modern cable carries BOTH sharp high-definition video AND audio from a laptop to a TV or projector?', 'HDMI cable', 'Mouse wire', 'Earphone jack', 'Power cord', 'a'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'At a supermarket checkout or school library, which handheld device reads black-and-white striped labels instantly?', 'Barcode Scanner', 'Microphone', 'Joystick', 'Cooling Pad', 'a'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Why can a laptop keep running during a power cut even without an external UPS?', 'Laptops have a built-in rechargeable battery inside', 'Laptops do not use electricity', 'The keyboard generates power', 'Laptops run on Wi-Fi waves', 'a'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What is the tiny removable storage card used inside many cameras and Android phones called?', 'Credit card', 'Graphics card', 'SIM card', 'MicroSD (Memory) card', 'd'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What is the main job of the small spinning fan inside a laptop or desktop cabinet?', 'To boost Wi-Fi signal', 'To make music louder', 'To keep the processor and internal parts cool so the computer does not overheat', 'To blow dust onto the screen', 'c'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'In everyday phones and computers, what is the simple difference between RAM and Storage (SSD/ROM)?', 'RAM stores photos forever; Storage deletes everything on restart', 'Both are names for the screen', 'RAM is only for printers', 'RAM holds active apps temporarily while working; Storage keeps your photos and files saved even when powered off', 'd'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'If your computer opens 15 browser tabs and starts feeling sluggish when switching apps, having more of which part helps most?', 'A louder speaker', 'A bigger mouse pad', 'RAM (working memory)', 'A longer power cable', 'c'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Modern laptops use an SSD instead of an older spinning Hard Disk (HDD). What everyday benefit do you notice right away?', 'It prints paper automatically', 'The screen becomes wider', 'The laptop boots up and opens apps much faster, with no moving disk parts', 'You never need to charge the battery', 'c'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)', 'PS/2 round port', 'CD-ROM slot', 'VGA port', 'a'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Whiteboard', 'Motherboard', 'Clipboard', 'Dashboard', 'b'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'If a wireless mouse stops moving the cursor on screen, what is the FIRST simple hardware thing you should check?', 'Check if its battery is low or its tiny power switch underneath is turned OFF', 'Reinstall Windows immediately', 'Delete your files', 'Buy a new monitor', 'a'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'A pen-like tool used by digital artists and students to write or draw neatly on a tablet screen is called a:', 'Router antenna', 'Thumb drive', 'Stylus', 'Laser printer', 'c'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which storage capacity is LARGER when comparing a pendrive or laptop storage?', '1 Kilobyte (1 KB)', '1 Megabyte (1 MB)', '1 Gigabyte (1 GB)', '1 Terabyte (1 TB)', 'd'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Roughly how many Gigabytes (GB) make 1 Terabyte (TB) on a hard drive?', 'About 1,000 GB (1,024 GB)', 'About 50 GB', 'About 2 GB', 'About 10 GB', 'a'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Before pulling out a USB pendrive while files are copying, why should you wait or click "Eject"?', 'It uses up Wi-Fi data', 'Otherwise the monitor turns black forever', 'Pulling it out mid-write can corrupt or damage the files being saved', 'The keyboard will lock', 'c'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Which computer component is specially helpful for smooth 3D video editing, animation, and modern games?', 'RJ45 plug', 'Floppy drive', 'GPU (Graphics Card / Graphics Processor)', 'Ink cartridge', 'c'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Why should you NEVER block the air vents on the bottom of a laptop by placing it deep into a thick blanket for hours?', 'It makes the screen brightness drop to zero', 'It deletes browser bookmarks', 'It disconnects Bluetooth earbuds', 'Blocked vents trap heat inside, causing overheating, slow performance, and battery wear', 'd'),
  (10, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'A desktop monitor is turned ON, its power light is blinking, and it says "No Signal." What is the most likely practical cause?', 'The internet website is down', 'Either the CPU cabinet is OFF or the HDMI/VGA display cable between the CPU and monitor is loose', 'Caps Lock is pressed on the keyboard', 'The Recycle Bin is full', 'b'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Which application is best suited for keeping an attendance list, marks table, or club budget with automatic totals?', 'Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets', 'MS Paint', 'Sound Recorder', 'Photos viewer', 'a'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What is the difference between "Copy & Paste" and "Cut & Paste" on a file?', 'Cut deletes the file permanently', 'Copy leaves the original file in place and makes a duplicate; Cut moves the file to the new folder', 'There is no difference', 'Copy works only on photos', 'b'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What is a ".zip" file commonly used for when sharing a project?', 'Charging laptop battery faster', 'Changing desktop wallpaper', 'Bundling many files/folders together into one smaller compressed file for easy sending', 'Making music play faster', 'c'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'In Word or Google Docs, what is the difference between "Save" and "Save As"?', 'Both print the document on paper', '"Save" only works offline', '"Save As" deletes the old file', '"Save" updates the current file; "Save As" lets you save a separate copy with a new name or location', 'd'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Which long bar at the bottom of a Windows screen shows the Start button, pinned apps, and clock?', 'Scroll bar', 'Formula bar', 'Bookmark bar', 'Taskbar', 'd'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Why do many students turn on "Dark Mode" in apps when reading or working in the evening?', 'It doubles storage space', 'It uses a dark background that feels gentler on the eyes in low light', 'It makes Wi-Fi twice as fast', 'It prints pages in black paper', 'b'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'If you want to jot down a quick plain-text note with zero heavy formatting, which lightweight built-in Windows app opens instantly?', 'Media Player', 'Device Manager', 'Notepad', 'Disk Defragmenter', 'c'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'When saving an image with a transparent background (such as a school logo), which image format supports transparency cleanly?', '.png', '.txt', '.exe', '.mp3', 'a'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'On Windows, files ending in ".exe" (or ".apk" on Android) are what kind of files?', 'Application installer / executable program files (only run from trusted official sources!)', 'Plain text essays', 'Family vacation photos', 'Spreadsheet charts', 'a'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'Before editing an important project presentation, why is naming files clearly like "Science_Poster_v2_Final.pptx" better than "asdf123.pptx"?', 'Computers refuse to save short names', 'Clear file names let you and your teammates find the right version in seconds without confusion', 'It changes slide colors automatically', 'Long names increase RAM', 'b'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'What does the "Spell Check" wavy red underline in Word or Google Docs indicate?', 'That the sentence will be deleted automatically', 'That the font is bold', 'A word that may have a spelling typo so you can review and fix it', 'That the computer has a virus', 'c'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'If a single app stops responding ("Not Responding") on Windows, how can you close JUST that stuck app without unplugging the whole PC?', 'Tap the monitor glass', 'Format the hard drive', 'Pull the electric plug from the wall', 'Open Task Manager, select the frozen app, and click "End Task"', 'd'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'What is "Open-Source Software" (such as Linux, VLC, Blender, or LibreOffice)?', 'Software that leaves your computer unlocked to strangers', 'Software that works only for 1 hour', 'Broken trial software', 'Software whose source code is openly shared so anyone can use, study, and improve it legally', 'd'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'When you install a new PDF app and Windows asks which "Default App" should open .pdf files, what does that setting control?', 'How fast the internet runs', 'Which program opens automatically whenever you double-click any .pdf file', 'Which user owns the computer', 'Whether printing is allowed', 'b'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'In Google Docs or Microsoft 365 Online, what is a huge everyday advantage of "Auto-Save" to the cloud?', 'It prints every page automatically', 'It writes your homework by itself', 'Your latest edits are saved continuously, so a sudden power cut does not wipe out an hour of typing', 'It works without turning on the screen', 'c'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'What is the purpose of Windows Security / Antivirus software on a PC?', 'To detect and block harmful malware or infected downloads before they damage your files', 'To edit birthday videos', 'To design school logos', 'To clean physical dust off the keyboard', 'a'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'Why do phones and laptops let you turn off unnecessary "Startup Apps" in Settings?', 'Fewer heavy apps launching automatically at boot makes the computer start up faster and saves memory', 'It uninstalls those apps permanently', 'It disables the keyboard', 'It turns off the screen color', 'a'),
  (10, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'When you download a `.zip` archive of club photos, why should you "Extract All" before editing the photos inside?', 'Otherwise the photos turn black and white', 'Extracting unpacks the compressed files into a normal folder so apps can open and save changes properly', 'Extracting doubles photo resolution', 'Zip files vanish after 5 minutes', 'b'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What does opening an "Incognito" or "Private" browser window ACTUALLY do on a shared computer?', 'It makes you completely invisible to websites and your internet provider', 'It stops the browser from saving your browsing history, cookies, and login session on THAT computer after you close the window', 'It blocks all computer viruses automatically', 'It gives free unlimited mobile data', 'b'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'If a webpage shows "404 — Page Not Found", what does that simply mean?', '404 people are viewing the site', 'Your laptop battery is at 4%', 'The specific link or page was moved, deleted, or typed with a spelling mistake', 'Your monitor is broken', 'c'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'When writing a polite email to a teacher or competition organizer, why should you always fill in the "Subject" line?', 'Subject hides your email address', 'Subject is where you type your password', 'Emails cannot be sent without 50 words in Subject', 'So the receiver immediately knows what your email is about before even opening it', 'd'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'If an expected registration confirmation email has not arrived in your Inbox, which email folder should you check next?', 'Drafts folder', 'Recycle Bin on Desktop', 'Downloads folder', 'Spam / Junk folder', 'd'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'Why do websites sometimes ask you to tick "I am not a robot" or pick traffic lights (CAPTCHA)?', 'To slow down your internet', 'To stop automated spam bots from creating fake accounts or flooding forms', 'To test your eyesight for driving', 'To update your browser', 'b'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'In Chrome or Edge, which shortcut opens your recent Downloads list directly inside the browser?', 'Alt + F4', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + J', 'Ctrl + U', 'c'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What are website "Cookies" in everyday browsing?', 'Tiny text files saved by websites in your browser to remember things like your login status or dark-mode preference', 'Free gift vouchers', 'Music playlists', 'Harmful hardware chips', 'a'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'In Google Search, putting quotation marks around an exact phrase like `"Maples Academy Khatauli"` helps you find:', 'Pages containing that exact phrase with those words together in that order', 'Only images and no text', 'Pages that do NOT mention Maples Academy', 'Only videos', 'a'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'What is Google Drive or Microsoft OneDrive an example of?', 'A physical pendrive inside your pocket', 'Cloud storage — lets you save files online and open or share them from any phone or computer', 'A computer cooling pad', 'An offline painting program', 'b'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'When sharing a Google Drive project link with your teacher, why should you check whether access is set to "Restricted" vs "Anyone with the link can View"?', 'View access lets anyone delete your account', 'Links only work on Sundays', 'If left "Restricted", your teacher will see "Access Denied" when clicking your submitted link!', 'Restricted links delete the file', 'c'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'On a noisy browser tab playing unexpected music, what does the tiny speaker icon on that tab let you see or do?', 'Print the tab', 'Bookmark the website', 'Record your microphone', 'Spot immediately which tab is playing sound and even mute that tab', 'd'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'What does an email ending in `.edu.in`, `.ac.in`, or `.gov.in` in India tell you about the website/sender?', 'Anyone can buy it anonymously for ₹10 without verification', 'It is a gaming server', 'It only works without internet', 'It belongs to a verified Indian educational institution (`.edu.in`/`.ac.in`) or government body (`.gov.in`)', 'd'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'If you start writing an email in Gmail and close the tab before clicking Send, where is your unfinished message saved automatically?', 'Sent', 'Drafts', 'Spam', 'Starred', 'b'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'What is a "Browser Extension" (or Add-on)?', 'A Wi-Fi booster antenna', 'An extra long charging cable', 'A small optional helper tool added inside your browser (which you should install ONLY from trusted creators)', 'A second monitor screen', 'c'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'If you want to save an online exam admit card or receipt neatly so you can view it offline anytime without internet, what can you select in the Print (`Ctrl + P`) destination menu?', 'Save as PDF', 'Bluetooth Speaker', 'Delete Page', 'Fax Machine', 'a'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'When a random flashy website suddenly asks "Allow this site to send you Notifications?", what is the smart habit if you do not need alerts from it?', 'Click "Block" — allowing shady sites to send notifications floods your screen with fake virus/ad pop-ups!', 'Always click Allow on every site', 'Enter your phone number', 'Restart your router', 'a'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'When sending an email announcement to 50 parents or students who do not know each other, why is `BCC` better than `CC`?', '`BCC` makes the email arrive faster', '`BCC` (Blind Carbon Copy) keeps everyone’s email address private from the other recipients', '`CC` deletes the email after reading', '`BCC` allows larger attachments', 'b'),
  (10, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'In an email thread sent to 40 club members, what happens if you click "Reply All" instead of "Reply"?', 'It deletes all previous emails', 'It translates your message', 'Your reply goes to ALL 40 people in the group instead of just the sender!', 'It replies only to yourself', 'c'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Internet plan speeds from providers like JioFiber, Airtel, or BSNL are commonly advertised in "100 Mbps". What does Mbps measure?', 'How many devices are allowed', 'How far the Wi-Fi reaches in meters', 'Megabits per second — how fast data transfers over your internet connection', 'How many months the plan lasts', 'c'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Companies like BSNL, Airtel, Jio, or local fiber broadband providers that connect homes/schools to the internet are called:', 'Operating Systems', 'Search Engines', 'Web Browsers', 'ISPs (Internet Service Providers)', 'd'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Why does Wi-Fi signal become weaker when you walk three rooms away behind thick concrete walls?', 'Wi-Fi needs sunlight to travel', 'The phone screen gets smaller', 'Gravity pulls Wi-Fi down', 'Thick walls and distance absorb and weaken wireless radio waves from the router', 'd'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'What is a "Local Area Network (LAN)" in simple everyday words?', 'A type of USB pendrive', 'Computers, laptops, and printers connected together inside one building, home, or school campus', 'Satellites orbiting Mars', 'An antivirus program', 'b'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'If ONE Wi-Fi printer is connected to the school office Wi-Fi router, how many computers on that same Wi-Fi can print to it?', 'Only phones with no SIM card', 'Zero — Wi-Fi printers cannot print', 'All authorized computers/phones on that same Wi-Fi network can share and print to it wirelessly', 'Only a computer plugged into it with an HDMI cable', 'c'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'When you mirror your phone or laptop screen wirelessly onto a classroom Smart TV without any cable, what is that feature called?', 'Screen Casting / Screen Mirroring', 'Zipping', 'Incognito Browsing', 'Disk Formatting', 'a'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Every device connected to a network gets an identifying number address (like a house number for delivering data packets). What is it called?', 'IP Address', 'PIN Code', 'Roll Number', 'Font Size', 'a'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'You are using a 1.5 GB/day mobile data pack via Hotspot. Watching 2 hours of video at `4K / 2160p` vs `480p` will do what?', '`4K` uses less data than `480p`', '`4K` uses many times more mobile data and can finish your 1.5 GB pack very quickly!', 'Resolution only affects audio volume', 'Both use zero mobile data', 'b'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It doubles keyboard speed', 'It uninstalls browsers', 'It pauses huge background Windows updates so your friend’s mobile data does not drain suddenly', 'It makes the screen brighter', 'c'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', 'There is no difference at all', '`2.4G` works only at 2:40 PM', '`5G` Wi-Fi requires a 5G SIM card inside the router', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', 'd'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What is "Quick Share / Nearby Share / AirDrop" on modern phones and laptops used for?', 'Charging another phone from 10 meters away', 'Deleting duplicate contacts', 'Scanning paper books', 'Sending photos or project files fast between two nearby devices wirelessly without wasting internet data', 'd'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Why should you avoid logging into banking or sensitive accounts on an open, password-free public Wi-Fi at a railway station or café?', 'Public Wi-Fi breaks your phone camera', 'Unsecured open Wi-Fi networks make it easier for attackers nearby to snoop on traffic or set up fake twin hotspots', 'Public Wi-Fi drains battery 10x faster', 'Public Wi-Fi deletes SIM contacts', 'b'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'In online video calls or multiplayer games, what does "High Ping / High Latency" (e.g., 450 ms instead of 25 ms) feel like?', 'More storage space', 'Extra crisp sound quality', 'A noticeable delay or lag between clicking/speaking and getting a response back', 'Higher screen brightness', 'c'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What brings ultrahigh-speed broadband into modern schools and homes using hair-thin strands of glass carrying pulses of light?', 'Fiber-Optic Cable', 'VGA Monitor Cable', 'Printer Ribbon', 'Aux Audio Cable', 'a'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'If the home internet suddenly stops working on ALL phones and laptops at once, what safe 1-minute step often resolves a stuck router?', 'Power-cycle the router: turn it OFF, wait 15–30 seconds, and turn it back ON', 'Factory-reset every phone in the house', 'Reinstall Windows', 'Cut the fiber cable', 'a'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What does "NFC" (Near Field Communication) on modern phones and smart cards allow?', 'Long-distance satellite TV reception', 'Tap-to-pay or instant pairing when held within a few centimeters of a reader/tag', 'Cooling the battery', 'Printing paper documents', 'b'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'When you type `mapleskhatauli.com` in your browser, which behind-the-scenes internet phonebook translates that friendly name into the server’s numeric IP address?', 'USB (Serial Bus)', 'PDF (Document Format)', 'DNS (Domain Name System)', 'UPS (Power Supply)', 'c'),
  (10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Your internet speed test shows `100 Mbps` (Megabits per second). Since 8 bits = 1 Byte, roughly how many Megabytes (`MB`) can download in 1 second?', '0.1 MB per second', '100 GB per second', 'Exactly 800 MB per second', 'Around 12.5 MB per second (`100 ÷ 8`)', 'd'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'There is zero risk', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'd'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'd'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Flashlights need your contacts to shine brighter', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Allow everything without reading', 'Give it microphone access too', 'b'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Cleaning computer fans', 'Searching for ocean documentaries online', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'Testing internet speed', 'c'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'a'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'a'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Click "Save" so you never have to type again', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'Share it with the café owner', 'Write your password on a sticky note on the monitor', 'b'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Starting personal arguments in front of 60 people', 'Forwarding unverified rumors', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Sending 80 stickers in a row at midnight', 'c'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To erase your photos', 'To slow down your internet', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'd'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'Change their account password', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'd'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Never read what you submit', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Assume computers can never be wrong', 'Turn off spell check', 'b'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'Batteries charge only when silent', 'Phones stop working after 10 PM', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'Night Wi-Fi costs double', 'c'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Click every link they sent', 'Keep it secret and worry alone', 'Send them your phone number to argue back', 'a'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'Saving a backup copy on a pendrive', 'Using open-source software legally', 'Checking spelling in Word', 'a'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Bend your neck 90 degrees inches from the keyboard', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low', 'Keep the monitor on the floor', 'Twist sideways on one leg', 'b'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '108', '139', '1930', '101', 'c'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'An encrypted ZIP file', 'A backup stored deep inside a folder', 'A high-resolution underwater nature video', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did', 'd'),
  (10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Transfer money within 10 seconds in panic', 'Share bank OTPs on the call', 'Install a screen-sharing app they suggest', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!', 'd'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Shift', 'Alt', 'Ctrl', 'Tab', 'a'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + M', 'c'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Closes the browser', 'Translates the page', 'Turns off Wi-Fi', 'Opens a new browser tab', 'd'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens Microsoft Word', 'Turns the screen white', 'Saves all bookmarks', 'a'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Scroll Lock', 'Pause/Break', 'Page Down', 'a'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F4', 'F8', 'F1', 'F2', 'd'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Turns on Bluetooth', 'Increases speaker volume', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Opens four new folders', 'c'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'Increases internet speed', 'Opens calculator', 'Adds a new user account', 'a'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Mutes computer sound', 'Deletes the webpage', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'Closes all tabs', 'c'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Closes the browser tab', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Submits the form immediately', 'Erases what you typed', 'b'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'If you step away from a computer for a minute, which Windows shortcut immediately LOCKS your screen?', 'Windows Key + L', 'Ctrl + L', 'Alt + L', 'Windows Key + O', 'a'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which Windows shortcut minimizes all open windows at once so you can see the Desktop?', 'Windows Key + D', 'Windows Key + P', 'Ctrl + D', 'Alt + D', 'a'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'You accidentally closed an important tab in Chrome/Edge! Which lifesaver shortcut reopens the last closed tab?', 'Ctrl + Alt + Z', 'Ctrl + Shift + T', 'Alt + Home', 'Shift + F5', 'b'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'What happens when you delete a file using Shift + Delete instead of just pressing Delete?', 'It moves the file to Desktop', 'Nothing happens', 'It copies the file twice', 'It permanently deletes the file without sending it to the Recycle Bin', 'd'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'Which Windows shortcut opens File Explorer ("This PC" / Folders) directly?', 'Alt + E', 'Ctrl + E', 'Windows Key + F', 'Windows Key + E', 'd'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'While typing a sentence, holding Ctrl and pressing Backspace (Ctrl + Backspace) erases what?', 'The entire word to the left of the cursor at once', 'The entire document', 'Only punctuation marks', 'Only one single letter', 'a'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'Which function key toggles Full-Screen mode ON or OFF in almost all web browsers?', 'F11', 'F3', 'F7', 'F1', 'a'),
  (11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'If a program freezes on Windows, which direct shortcut opens Task Manager immediately?', 'Windows Key + M', 'Ctrl + Alt + P', 'Ctrl + Shift + Esc', 'Shift + Tab', 'c'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What is the main job of the small spinning fan inside a laptop or desktop cabinet?', 'To boost Wi-Fi signal', 'To keep the processor and internal parts cool so the computer does not overheat', 'To blow dust onto the screen', 'To make music louder', 'b'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'In everyday phones and computers, what is the simple difference between RAM and Storage (SSD/ROM)?', 'RAM holds active apps temporarily while working; Storage keeps your photos and files saved even when powered off', 'Both are names for the screen', 'RAM is only for printers', 'RAM stores photos forever; Storage deletes everything on restart', 'a'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'If your computer opens 15 browser tabs and starts feeling sluggish when switching apps, having more of which part helps most?', 'A bigger mouse pad', 'RAM (working memory)', 'A louder speaker', 'A longer power cable', 'b'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Modern laptops use an SSD instead of an older spinning Hard Disk (HDD). What everyday benefit do you notice right away?', 'The screen becomes wider', 'The laptop boots up and opens apps much faster, with no moving disk parts', 'It prints paper automatically', 'You never need to charge the battery', 'b'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'PS/2 round port', 'CD-ROM slot', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)', 'VGA port', 'c'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Dashboard', 'Clipboard', 'Motherboard', 'Whiteboard', 'c'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'If a wireless mouse stops moving the cursor on screen, what is the FIRST simple hardware thing you should check?', 'Check if its battery is low or its tiny power switch underneath is turned OFF', 'Buy a new monitor', 'Delete your files', 'Reinstall Windows immediately', 'a'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'A pen-like tool used by digital artists and students to write or draw neatly on a tablet screen is called a:', 'Router antenna', 'Stylus', 'Laser printer', 'Thumb drive', 'b'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which storage capacity is LARGER when comparing a pendrive or laptop storage?', '1 Kilobyte (1 KB)', '1 Gigabyte (1 GB)', '1 Terabyte (1 TB)', '1 Megabyte (1 MB)', 'c'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Roughly how many Gigabytes (GB) make 1 Terabyte (TB) on a hard drive?', 'About 10 GB', 'About 50 GB', 'About 2 GB', 'About 1,000 GB (1,024 GB)', 'd'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Before pulling out a USB pendrive while files are copying, why should you wait or click "Eject"?', 'Otherwise the monitor turns black forever', 'Pulling it out mid-write can corrupt or damage the files being saved', 'It uses up Wi-Fi data', 'The keyboard will lock', 'b'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which computer component is specially helpful for smooth 3D video editing, animation, and modern games?', 'Floppy drive', 'GPU (Graphics Card / Graphics Processor)', 'RJ45 plug', 'Ink cartridge', 'b'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Why should you NEVER block the air vents on the bottom of a laptop by placing it deep into a thick blanket for hours?', 'It deletes browser bookmarks', 'It disconnects Bluetooth earbuds', 'It makes the screen brightness drop to zero', 'Blocked vents trap heat inside, causing overheating, slow performance, and battery wear', 'd'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'A desktop monitor is turned ON, its power light is blinking, and it says "No Signal." What is the most likely practical cause?', 'The Recycle Bin is full', 'Caps Lock is pressed on the keyboard', 'Either the CPU cabinet is OFF or the HDMI/VGA display cable between the CPU and monitor is loose', 'The internet website is down', 'c'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'What is the difference between putting a laptop to "Sleep" versus "Shut Down"?', 'Sleep erases all saved files', 'Shut Down uses more battery than playing games', 'Both are identical', 'Sleep keeps open work ready in low-power memory for instant wake-up; Shut Down closes everything completely', 'd'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'What does screen resolution like "1920 × 1080 (Full HD)" describe on a monitor or phone?', 'How many files can fit on the desktop', 'The weight of the monitor in grams', 'The grid of tiny pixels (width × height) that makes up the sharpness of the display', 'How loud the speakers are', 'c'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'An "All-in-One" desktop PC in a modern lab has no separate tower box on the desk. Where are its processor, RAM, and SSD located?', 'On the internet cloud only', 'Built neatly right behind the monitor screen itself', 'Inside the mouse', 'Inside the keyboard spacebar', 'b'),
  (11, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Why do ink-tank or laser printers usually cost much less per page for a school office than tiny cheap ink-cartridge printers?', 'They do not use paper', 'They only print on Sundays', 'They require no electricity', 'Refill ink bottles and toner print thousands of pages at a fraction of the cost per page', 'd'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Which long bar at the bottom of a Windows screen shows the Start button, pinned apps, and clock?', 'Taskbar', 'Formula bar', 'Bookmark bar', 'Scroll bar', 'a'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Why do many students turn on "Dark Mode" in apps when reading or working in the evening?', 'It uses a dark background that feels gentler on the eyes in low light', 'It makes Wi-Fi twice as fast', 'It doubles storage space', 'It prints pages in black paper', 'a'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'If you want to jot down a quick plain-text note with zero heavy formatting, which lightweight built-in Windows app opens instantly?', 'Device Manager', 'Notepad', 'Media Player', 'Disk Defragmenter', 'b'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'When saving an image with a transparent background (such as a school logo), which image format supports transparency cleanly?', '.txt', '.exe', '.png', '.mp3', 'c'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'On Windows, files ending in ".exe" (or ".apk" on Android) are what kind of files?', 'Spreadsheet charts', 'Family vacation photos', 'Plain text essays', 'Application installer / executable program files (only run from trusted official sources!)', 'd'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Before editing an important project presentation, why is naming files clearly like "Science_Poster_v2_Final.pptx" better than "asdf123.pptx"?', 'Computers refuse to save short names', 'Long names increase RAM', 'It changes slide colors automatically', 'Clear file names let you and your teammates find the right version in seconds without confusion', 'd'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What does the "Spell Check" wavy red underline in Word or Google Docs indicate?', 'That the sentence will be deleted automatically', 'A word that may have a spelling typo so you can review and fix it', 'That the computer has a virus', 'That the font is bold', 'b'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'If a single app stops responding ("Not Responding") on Windows, how can you close JUST that stuck app without unplugging the whole PC?', 'Tap the monitor glass', 'Pull the electric plug from the wall', 'Open Task Manager, select the frozen app, and click "End Task"', 'Format the hard drive', 'c'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'What is "Open-Source Software" (such as Linux, VLC, Blender, or LibreOffice)?', 'Software whose source code is openly shared so anyone can use, study, and improve it legally', 'Software that works only for 1 hour', 'Broken trial software', 'Software that leaves your computer unlocked to strangers', 'a'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'When you install a new PDF app and Windows asks which "Default App" should open .pdf files, what does that setting control?', 'Which program opens automatically whenever you double-click any .pdf file', 'Which user owns the computer', 'How fast the internet runs', 'Whether printing is allowed', 'a'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'In Google Docs or Microsoft 365 Online, what is a huge everyday advantage of "Auto-Save" to the cloud?', 'It writes your homework by itself', 'Your latest edits are saved continuously, so a sudden power cut does not wipe out an hour of typing', 'It prints every page automatically', 'It works without turning on the screen', 'b'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'What is the purpose of Windows Security / Antivirus software on a PC?', 'To edit birthday videos', 'To design school logos', 'To detect and block harmful malware or infected downloads before they damage your files', 'To clean physical dust off the keyboard', 'c'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'Why do phones and laptops let you turn off unnecessary "Startup Apps" in Settings?', 'It turns off the screen color', 'It disables the keyboard', 'It uninstalls those apps permanently', 'Fewer heavy apps launching automatically at boot makes the computer start up faster and saves memory', 'd'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'When you download a `.zip` archive of club photos, why should you "Extract All" before editing the photos inside?', 'Otherwise the photos turn black and white', 'Zip files vanish after 5 minutes', 'Extracting doubles photo resolution', 'Extracting unpacks the compressed files into a normal folder so apps can open and save changes properly', 'd'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'What does "Version History" in Google Docs, Slides, or Sheets let a student team do?', 'Check the laptop manufacturing year', 'See earlier saved versions of a document and restore work if someone accidentally erased a section', 'See every website visited on the computer', 'Speed up the CPU', 'b'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'If you copy a song file onto your Desktop as a "Shortcut" (tiny arrow on the icon) and then copy ONLY that shortcut to a pendrive, what happens at school?', 'It converts the song into a video', 'It plays twice as loud', 'It will NOT play, because a shortcut is only a pointer link — not the actual `.mp3` song file itself!', 'It copies your entire computer', 'c'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'What is a `.csv` (Comma-Separated Values) file commonly used for between apps like Excel, Google Sheets, and portals?', 'Importing or exporting simple clean rows and columns of table data (like student lists or questions)', 'Recording voice notes', 'Editing photo brightness', 'Playing 3D animations', 'a'),
  (11, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'On a phone or computer, what is the difference between "Clearing App Cache" and "Clearing App Data / Storage"?', 'Clearing Cache removes temporary files safely; Clearing Data resets the app like a fresh install and logs you out', 'Clearing Cache deletes all your contacts', 'Both uninstall the operating system', 'Neither frees any space', 'a'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'Why do websites sometimes ask you to tick "I am not a robot" or pick traffic lights (CAPTCHA)?', 'To stop automated spam bots from creating fake accounts or flooding forms', 'To test your eyesight for driving', 'To slow down your internet', 'To update your browser', 'a'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'In Chrome or Edge, which shortcut opens your recent Downloads list directly inside the browser?', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + J', 'Alt + F4', 'Ctrl + U', 'b'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What are website "Cookies" in everyday browsing?', 'Free gift vouchers', 'Music playlists', 'Tiny text files saved by websites in your browser to remember things like your login status or dark-mode preference', 'Harmful hardware chips', 'c'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'In Google Search, putting quotation marks around an exact phrase like `"Maples Academy Khatauli"` helps you find:', 'Only videos', 'Pages that do NOT mention Maples Academy', 'Only images and no text', 'Pages containing that exact phrase with those words together in that order', 'd'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What is Google Drive or Microsoft OneDrive an example of?', 'A physical pendrive inside your pocket', 'An offline painting program', 'A computer cooling pad', 'Cloud storage — lets you save files online and open or share them from any phone or computer', 'd'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'When sharing a Google Drive project link with your teacher, why should you check whether access is set to "Restricted" vs "Anyone with the link can View"?', 'View access lets anyone delete your account', 'If left "Restricted", your teacher will see "Access Denied" when clicking your submitted link!', 'Restricted links delete the file', 'Links only work on Sundays', 'b'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'On a noisy browser tab playing unexpected music, what does the tiny speaker icon on that tab let you see or do?', 'Print the tab', 'Record your microphone', 'Spot immediately which tab is playing sound and even mute that tab', 'Bookmark the website', 'c'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'What does an email ending in `.edu.in`, `.ac.in`, or `.gov.in` in India tell you about the website/sender?', 'It belongs to a verified Indian educational institution (`.edu.in`/`.ac.in`) or government body (`.gov.in`)', 'It is a gaming server', 'It only works without internet', 'Anyone can buy it anonymously for ₹10 without verification', 'a'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'If you start writing an email in Gmail and close the tab before clicking Send, where is your unfinished message saved automatically?', 'Drafts', 'Spam', 'Sent', 'Starred', 'a'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'What is a "Browser Extension" (or Add-on)?', 'An extra long charging cable', 'A small optional helper tool added inside your browser (which you should install ONLY from trusted creators)', 'A Wi-Fi booster antenna', 'A second monitor screen', 'b'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'If you want to save an online exam admit card or receipt neatly so you can view it offline anytime without internet, what can you select in the Print (`Ctrl + P`) destination menu?', 'Bluetooth Speaker', 'Delete Page', 'Save as PDF', 'Fax Machine', 'c'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'When a random flashy website suddenly asks "Allow this site to send you Notifications?", what is the smart habit if you do not need alerts from it?', 'Restart your router', 'Enter your phone number', 'Always click Allow on every site', 'Click "Block" — allowing shady sites to send notifications floods your screen with fake virus/ad pop-ups!', 'd'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'When sending an email announcement to 50 parents or students who do not know each other, why is `BCC` better than `CC`?', '`BCC` makes the email arrive faster', '`BCC` allows larger attachments', '`CC` deletes the email after reading', '`BCC` (Blind Carbon Copy) keeps everyone’s email address private from the other recipients', 'd'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'In an email thread sent to 40 club members, what happens if you click "Reply All" instead of "Reply"?', 'It deletes all previous emails', 'Your reply goes to ALL 40 people in the group instead of just the sender!', 'It replies only to yourself', 'It translates your message', 'b'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'Look closely at two URLs: `https://sbi.co.in` vs `https://sbi-login-kyc.freehost.xyz`. In the second URL, which company actually owns the real website domain?', 'Google', 'State Bank of India', '`freehost.xyz` — the `sbi-login-kyc` part at the front is just a fake subdomain trick!', 'Reserve Bank of India', 'c'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'If a webpage looks broken or keeps showing an outdated version even after refreshing, what browser step usually fixes it?', 'Hard Refresh (`Ctrl + F5`) or clearing cached images and files for that site', 'Uninstalling Microsoft Word', 'Lowering speaker volume', 'Replacing the mouse', 'a'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'In Chrome/Edge, why is creating separate "Browser Profiles" helpful when two siblings share one home laptop?', 'Each sibling gets their own separate bookmarks, history, and logged-in school accounts without mixing them up', 'It doubles the laptop hard disk size', 'It creates two physical screens', 'It makes Wi-Fi free', 'a'),
  (11, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'Why shouldn’t you blindly trust a shortened mystery link (like `bit.ly/3xYz99`) sent by an unknown stranger?', 'Short links only work on desktop PCs', 'Shortened links hide the real destination website URL until clicked, so they can disguise phishing or scam sites', 'Short links turn off Bluetooth', 'Short links use 10 GB of data', 'b'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'If ONE Wi-Fi printer is connected to the school office Wi-Fi router, how many computers on that same Wi-Fi can print to it?', 'Zero — Wi-Fi printers cannot print', 'All authorized computers/phones on that same Wi-Fi network can share and print to it wirelessly', 'Only phones with no SIM card', 'Only a computer plugged into it with an HDMI cable', 'b'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'When you mirror your phone or laptop screen wirelessly onto a classroom Smart TV without any cable, what is that feature called?', 'Zipping', 'Incognito Browsing', 'Screen Casting / Screen Mirroring', 'Disk Formatting', 'c'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Every device connected to a network gets an identifying number address (like a house number for delivering data packets). What is it called?', 'Font Size', 'Roll Number', 'PIN Code', 'IP Address', 'd'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'You are using a 1.5 GB/day mobile data pack via Hotspot. Watching 2 hours of video at `4K / 2160p` vs `480p` will do what?', '`4K` uses less data than `480p`', 'Both use zero mobile data', 'Resolution only affects audio volume', '`4K` uses many times more mobile data and can finish your 1.5 GB pack very quickly!', 'd'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It doubles keyboard speed', 'It pauses huge background Windows updates so your friend’s mobile data does not drain suddenly', 'It makes the screen brighter', 'It uninstalls browsers', 'b'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', 'There is no difference at all', '`5G` Wi-Fi requires a 5G SIM card inside the router', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', '`2.4G` works only at 2:40 PM', 'c'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'What is "Quick Share / Nearby Share / AirDrop" on modern phones and laptops used for?', 'Sending photos or project files fast between two nearby devices wirelessly without wasting internet data', 'Deleting duplicate contacts', 'Scanning paper books', 'Charging another phone from 10 meters away', 'a'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Why should you avoid logging into banking or sensitive accounts on an open, password-free public Wi-Fi at a railway station or café?', 'Unsecured open Wi-Fi networks make it easier for attackers nearby to snoop on traffic or set up fake twin hotspots', 'Public Wi-Fi drains battery 10x faster', 'Public Wi-Fi breaks your phone camera', 'Public Wi-Fi deletes SIM contacts', 'a'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'In online video calls or multiplayer games, what does "High Ping / High Latency" (e.g., 450 ms instead of 25 ms) feel like?', 'Extra crisp sound quality', 'A noticeable delay or lag between clicking/speaking and getting a response back', 'More storage space', 'Higher screen brightness', 'b'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What brings ultrahigh-speed broadband into modern schools and homes using hair-thin strands of glass carrying pulses of light?', 'VGA Monitor Cable', 'Printer Ribbon', 'Fiber-Optic Cable', 'Aux Audio Cable', 'c'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'If the home internet suddenly stops working on ALL phones and laptops at once, what safe 1-minute step often resolves a stuck router?', 'Cut the fiber cable', 'Reinstall Windows', 'Factory-reset every phone in the house', 'Power-cycle the router: turn it OFF, wait 15–30 seconds, and turn it back ON', 'd'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What does "NFC" (Near Field Communication) on modern phones and smart cards allow?', 'Long-distance satellite TV reception', 'Printing paper documents', 'Cooling the battery', 'Tap-to-pay or instant pairing when held within a few centimeters of a reader/tag', 'd'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'When you type `mapleskhatauli.com` in your browser, which behind-the-scenes internet phonebook translates that friendly name into the server’s numeric IP address?', 'USB (Serial Bus)', 'DNS (Domain Name System)', 'UPS (Power Supply)', 'PDF (Document Format)', 'b'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Your internet speed test shows `100 Mbps` (Megabits per second). Since 8 bits = 1 Byte, roughly how many Megabytes (`MB`) can download in 1 second?', '0.1 MB per second', 'Exactly 800 MB per second', 'Around 12.5 MB per second (`100 ÷ 8`)', '100 GB per second', 'c'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Why is setting up a separate "Guest Wi-Fi" network on a home or school router a smart security practice for visitors?', 'Visitors get internet access while keeping your main school/home computers and shared printers isolated and private', 'Guest Wi-Fi doubles your ISP plan speed', 'Guest Wi-Fi works 5 km away', 'Guest Wi-Fi needs no electricity', 'a'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What is "USB Tethering" between a smartphone and a desktop PC that has no Wi-Fi adapter?', 'Sharing your phone’s internet connection directly to the desktop PC through a normal USB charging/data cable!', 'Tying the phone to the desk with a rope', 'Printing photos directly from SIM card', 'Formatting the phone', 'a'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What is the role of a "Firewall" in Windows or a school router?', 'It prevents physical fire in the computer room', 'It monitors incoming and outgoing network traffic and blocks unauthorized outside connections', 'It deletes old browser bookmarks', 'It heats up the CPU in winter', 'b'),
  (11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Why should you change the default admin login (`admin / admin`) printed on the bottom sticker of a new home Wi-Fi router?', 'Default passwords use more electricity', 'It voids the monitor warranty', 'Anyone connected nearby who knows common default logins could open router settings and change your Wi-Fi or DNS!', 'Otherwise Wi-Fi turns off after 24 hours', 'c'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'c'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'd'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Click "Save" so you never have to type again', 'Write your password on a sticky note on the monitor', 'Share it with the café owner', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'd'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Starting personal arguments in front of 60 people', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Sending 80 stickers in a row at midnight', 'Forwarding unverified rumors', 'b'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To erase your photos', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'To slow down your internet', 'c'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'Change their account password', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'a'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Assume computers can never be wrong', 'Never read what you submit', 'Turn off spell check', 'a'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'Phones stop working after 10 PM', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'Batteries charge only when silent', 'Night Wi-Fi costs double', 'b'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Click every link they sent', 'Keep it secret and worry alone', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Send them your phone number to argue back', 'c'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Checking spelling in Word', 'Using open-source software legally', 'Saving a backup copy on a pendrive', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'd'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Bend your neck 90 degrees inches from the keyboard', 'Twist sideways on one leg', 'Keep the monitor on the floor', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low', 'd'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '108', '1930', '101', '139', 'b'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'An encrypted ZIP file', 'A high-resolution underwater nature video', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did', 'A backup stored deep inside a folder', 'c'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!', 'Share bank OTPs on the call', 'Install a screen-sharing app they suggest', 'Transfer money within 10 seconds in panic', 'a'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why do scammers urgently ask victims to install remote screen-sharing apps (like AnyDesk / TeamViewer / unknown `.apk`s) during fake "KYC / customer care" calls?', 'Because screen-sharing lets the scammer see your live phone screen, including incoming bank OTPs and apps!', 'To clean dust from your phone speaker', 'To double your mobile battery life', 'Banks require AnyDesk for every account', 'a'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'When designing a club registration form (Data Minimization principle), which information is ethical and sensible to collect?', 'Parents’ bank account numbers and Aadhaar passwords', 'Only what is genuinely needed for the club (Name, Roll No, Class, Section) — never unnecessary private family/financial data!', 'Personal email passwords', 'Home Wi-Fi passwords of every student', 'b'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What does a "Creative Commons (CC)" license on an online photo or music track tell students making a video project?', 'Nobody is allowed to view the image', 'You can sell it as your own painting without credit', 'The creator has given clear permission to reuse the work under stated conditions (such as giving proper attribution/credit)', 'The file contains a virus', 'c'),
  (11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What should families do with old dead batteries, broken chargers, and discarded electronics ("E-Waste") instead of burning them or tossing them in open drains?', 'Break screens with a hammer in class', 'Throw batteries into rivers', 'Burn plastic circuit boards in the backyard', 'Hand them over to authorized E-Waste collection/recycling centers so toxic metals don’t pollute soil and water', 'd'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Page Down', 'Pause/Break', 'Scroll Lock', 'a'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F4', 'F1', 'F2', 'F8', 'c'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Turns on Bluetooth', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Opens four new folders', 'Increases speaker volume', 'b'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Adds a new user account', 'Increases internet speed', 'Opens calculator', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'd'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Deletes the webpage', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'Mutes computer sound', 'Closes all tabs', 'b'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Submits the form immediately', 'Closes the browser tab', 'Erases what you typed', 'a'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'If you step away from a computer for a minute, which Windows shortcut immediately LOCKS your screen?', 'Ctrl + L', 'Alt + L', 'Windows Key + L', 'Windows Key + O', 'c'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which Windows shortcut minimizes all open windows at once so you can see the Desktop?', 'Alt + D', 'Ctrl + D', 'Windows Key + P', 'Windows Key + D', 'd'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'You accidentally closed an important tab in Chrome/Edge! Which lifesaver shortcut reopens the last closed tab?', 'Ctrl + Alt + Z', 'Shift + F5', 'Alt + Home', 'Ctrl + Shift + T', 'd'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'What happens when you delete a file using Shift + Delete instead of just pressing Delete?', 'It moves the file to Desktop', 'It copies the file twice', 'It permanently deletes the file without sending it to the Recycle Bin', 'Nothing happens', 'c'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which Windows shortcut opens File Explorer ("This PC" / Folders) directly?', 'Alt + E', 'Windows Key + F', 'Windows Key + E', 'Ctrl + E', 'c'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'While typing a sentence, holding Ctrl and pressing Backspace (Ctrl + Backspace) erases what?', 'Only one single letter', 'The entire document', 'Only punctuation marks', 'The entire word to the left of the cursor at once', 'd'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which function key toggles Full-Screen mode ON or OFF in almost all web browsers?', 'F3', 'F7', 'F11', 'F1', 'c'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'If a program freezes on Windows, which direct shortcut opens Task Manager immediately?', 'Ctrl + Alt + P', 'Ctrl + Shift + Esc', 'Windows Key + M', 'Shift + Tab', 'b'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'Which modern Windows shortcut lets you drag and capture a screenshot of just ONE selected area of your screen?', 'Alt + S', 'Ctrl + F4', 'Windows Key + Shift + S', 'Ctrl + P', 'c'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In Word, Google Docs, or Notepad, which shortcut opens "Find and Replace" to swap a repeated word across the whole file?', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + J', 'Ctrl + H', 'd'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In a web browser, pressing Ctrl + L (or Alt + D) quickly highlights what?', 'The top Address / URL bar so you can type a website or search immediately', 'Your computer wallpaper', 'The Recycle Bin', 'The bottom footer of the webpage', 'a'),
  (12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In Word, Google Docs, or email apps, pressing Ctrl + K on selected text lets you insert what?', 'An audio recording', 'A clickable hyperlink (website link)', 'A page break', 'A password lock', 'b'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'PS/2 round port', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)', 'VGA port', 'CD-ROM slot', 'b'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Dashboard', 'Motherboard', 'Whiteboard', 'Clipboard', 'b'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'If a wireless mouse stops moving the cursor on screen, what is the FIRST simple hardware thing you should check?', 'Reinstall Windows immediately', 'Buy a new monitor', 'Delete your files', 'Check if its battery is low or its tiny power switch underneath is turned OFF', 'd'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'A pen-like tool used by digital artists and students to write or draw neatly on a tablet screen is called a:', 'Stylus', 'Laser printer', 'Router antenna', 'Thumb drive', 'a'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which storage capacity is LARGER when comparing a pendrive or laptop storage?', '1 Gigabyte (1 GB)', '1 Terabyte (1 TB)', '1 Kilobyte (1 KB)', '1 Megabyte (1 MB)', 'b'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Roughly how many Gigabytes (GB) make 1 Terabyte (TB) on a hard drive?', 'About 50 GB', 'About 2 GB', 'About 10 GB', 'About 1,000 GB (1,024 GB)', 'd'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Before pulling out a USB pendrive while files are copying, why should you wait or click "Eject"?', 'The keyboard will lock', 'It uses up Wi-Fi data', 'Pulling it out mid-write can corrupt or damage the files being saved', 'Otherwise the monitor turns black forever', 'c'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which computer component is specially helpful for smooth 3D video editing, animation, and modern games?', 'Floppy drive', 'Ink cartridge', 'RJ45 plug', 'GPU (Graphics Card / Graphics Processor)', 'd'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Why should you NEVER block the air vents on the bottom of a laptop by placing it deep into a thick blanket for hours?', 'It deletes browser bookmarks', 'It makes the screen brightness drop to zero', 'Blocked vents trap heat inside, causing overheating, slow performance, and battery wear', 'It disconnects Bluetooth earbuds', 'c'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'A desktop monitor is turned ON, its power light is blinking, and it says "No Signal." What is the most likely practical cause?', 'The Recycle Bin is full', 'Either the CPU cabinet is OFF or the HDMI/VGA display cable between the CPU and monitor is loose', 'The internet website is down', 'Caps Lock is pressed on the keyboard', 'b'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the difference between putting a laptop to "Sleep" versus "Shut Down"?', 'Sleep keeps open work ready in low-power memory for instant wake-up; Shut Down closes everything completely', 'Shut Down uses more battery than playing games', 'Both are identical', 'Sleep erases all saved files', 'a'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What does screen resolution like "1920 × 1080 (Full HD)" describe on a monitor or phone?', 'The weight of the monitor in grams', 'The grid of tiny pixels (width × height) that makes up the sharpness of the display', 'How many files can fit on the desktop', 'How loud the speakers are', 'b'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'An "All-in-One" desktop PC in a modern lab has no separate tower box on the desk. Where are its processor, RAM, and SSD located?', 'Built neatly right behind the monitor screen itself', 'Inside the mouse', 'On the internet cloud only', 'Inside the keyboard spacebar', 'a'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Why do ink-tank or laser printers usually cost much less per page for a school office than tiny cheap ink-cartridge printers?', 'They only print on Sundays', 'They require no electricity', 'They do not use paper', 'Refill ink bottles and toner print thousands of pages at a fraction of the cost per page', 'd'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'What does a "60Hz" vs "120Hz" refresh rate on a phone or monitor screen mean in everyday use?', 'The Wi-Fi password length', 'How many apps can be installed', 'How many hours the battery lasts', 'How many times per second the screen updates the image — higher feels smoother while scrolling', 'd'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'On headphones with a single 3.5mm plug (TRRS) used on laptops and phones, what does that single plug carry?', 'Internet Wi-Fi signal', 'Printer ink levels', 'Screen brightness power', 'Left audio, Right audio, AND Microphone voice signal together', 'd'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'What is "Surge Protection" on a good computer extension spike-guard?', 'A tool that blocks pop-up ads', 'A feature that speeds up typing', 'Protection that shields connected computers from sudden high-voltage electricity spikes', 'A waterproof cover for monitors', 'c'),
  (12, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'If your phone says "Storage Almost Full (98% used)", which action frees up real internal storage space?', 'Changing the lock-screen wallpaper', 'Backing up large old videos/downloads to cloud or PC and deleting unneeded heavy files/apps', 'Lowering screen brightness', 'Turning on Airplane Mode', 'b'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'On Windows, files ending in ".exe" (or ".apk" on Android) are what kind of files?', 'Spreadsheet charts', 'Plain text essays', 'Application installer / executable program files (only run from trusted official sources!)', 'Family vacation photos', 'c'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Before editing an important project presentation, why is naming files clearly like "Science_Poster_v2_Final.pptx" better than "asdf123.pptx"?', 'Clear file names let you and your teammates find the right version in seconds without confusion', 'Long names increase RAM', 'It changes slide colors automatically', 'Computers refuse to save short names', 'a'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What does the "Spell Check" wavy red underline in Word or Google Docs indicate?', 'A word that may have a spelling typo so you can review and fix it', 'That the computer has a virus', 'That the sentence will be deleted automatically', 'That the font is bold', 'a'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'If a single app stops responding ("Not Responding") on Windows, how can you close JUST that stuck app without unplugging the whole PC?', 'Pull the electric plug from the wall', 'Open Task Manager, select the frozen app, and click "End Task"', 'Tap the monitor glass', 'Format the hard drive', 'b'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What is "Open-Source Software" (such as Linux, VLC, Blender, or LibreOffice)?', 'Software that works only for 1 hour', 'Broken trial software', 'Software whose source code is openly shared so anyone can use, study, and improve it legally', 'Software that leaves your computer unlocked to strangers', 'c'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'When you install a new PDF app and Windows asks which "Default App" should open .pdf files, what does that setting control?', 'Whether printing is allowed', 'How fast the internet runs', 'Which user owns the computer', 'Which program opens automatically whenever you double-click any .pdf file', 'd'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'In Google Docs or Microsoft 365 Online, what is a huge everyday advantage of "Auto-Save" to the cloud?', 'It writes your homework by itself', 'It works without turning on the screen', 'It prints every page automatically', 'Your latest edits are saved continuously, so a sudden power cut does not wipe out an hour of typing', 'd'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'What is the purpose of Windows Security / Antivirus software on a PC?', 'To edit birthday videos', 'To detect and block harmful malware or infected downloads before they damage your files', 'To clean physical dust off the keyboard', 'To design school logos', 'b'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'Why do phones and laptops let you turn off unnecessary "Startup Apps" in Settings?', 'It turns off the screen color', 'It uninstalls those apps permanently', 'Fewer heavy apps launching automatically at boot makes the computer start up faster and saves memory', 'It disables the keyboard', 'c'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'When you download a `.zip` archive of club photos, why should you "Extract All" before editing the photos inside?', 'Extracting unpacks the compressed files into a normal folder so apps can open and save changes properly', 'Zip files vanish after 5 minutes', 'Extracting doubles photo resolution', 'Otherwise the photos turn black and white', 'a'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'What does "Version History" in Google Docs, Slides, or Sheets let a student team do?', 'See earlier saved versions of a document and restore work if someone accidentally erased a section', 'See every website visited on the computer', 'Check the laptop manufacturing year', 'Speed up the CPU', 'a'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'If you copy a song file onto your Desktop as a "Shortcut" (tiny arrow on the icon) and then copy ONLY that shortcut to a pendrive, what happens at school?', 'It plays twice as loud', 'It will NOT play, because a shortcut is only a pointer link — not the actual `.mp3` song file itself!', 'It converts the song into a video', 'It copies your entire computer', 'b'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'What is a `.csv` (Comma-Separated Values) file commonly used for between apps like Excel, Google Sheets, and portals?', 'Recording voice notes', 'Editing photo brightness', 'Importing or exporting simple clean rows and columns of table data (like student lists or questions)', 'Playing 3D animations', 'c'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'medium', 'On a phone or computer, what is the difference between "Clearing App Cache" and "Clearing App Data / Storage"?', 'Neither frees any space', 'Both uninstall the operating system', 'Clearing Cache deletes all your contacts', 'Clearing Cache removes temporary files safely; Clearing Data resets the app like a fresh install and logs you out', 'd'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'Why is "Restarting" a computer sometimes more helpful than "Shut Down and Turn On" when fixing a minor software glitch?', 'Restart charges the battery to 100%', 'Restart upgrades the monitor size', 'Restart deletes old emails', 'Restart performs a clean full reload of the operating system and drivers from scratch', 'd'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'What does "Cloud Sync" (like Google Drive, OneDrive, or Google Photos backup) protect you from?', 'Running out of printer ink', 'Losing your important school projects or photos if your phone or pendrive gets lost or damaged', 'Screen scratches if dropped', 'Keyboard key dust', 'b'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'When printing a 20-page document and you only need Page 3 and Page 4, what should you choose in the Print dialog?', 'Turn off the printer mid-way', 'Print all 20 pages and throw 18 away', 'Select "Custom Pages" and type `3-4` so you do not waste 18 extra sheets of paper', 'Delete the other 18 pages from your original file', 'c'),
  (12, 'Application Software & OS', 'hard', 'What does "Portrait" vs "Landscape" orientation mean when printing a certificate or poster?', 'Portrait is tall/vertical (like a book page); Landscape is wide/horizontal (like a certificate)', 'Portrait is color; Landscape is black-and-white', 'Both print sideways', 'Portrait prints only faces; Landscape prints only trees', 'a'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What is Google Drive or Microsoft OneDrive an example of?', 'Cloud storage — lets you save files online and open or share them from any phone or computer', 'An offline painting program', 'A computer cooling pad', 'A physical pendrive inside your pocket', 'a'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'When sharing a Google Drive project link with your teacher, why should you check whether access is set to "Restricted" vs "Anyone with the link can View"?', 'If left "Restricted", your teacher will see "Access Denied" when clicking your submitted link!', 'Restricted links delete the file', 'View access lets anyone delete your account', 'Links only work on Sundays', 'a'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'On a noisy browser tab playing unexpected music, what does the tiny speaker icon on that tab let you see or do?', 'Record your microphone', 'Spot immediately which tab is playing sound and even mute that tab', 'Print the tab', 'Bookmark the website', 'b'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What does an email ending in `.edu.in`, `.ac.in`, or `.gov.in` in India tell you about the website/sender?', 'It is a gaming server', 'It only works without internet', 'It belongs to a verified Indian educational institution (`.edu.in`/`.ac.in`) or government body (`.gov.in`)', 'Anyone can buy it anonymously for ₹10 without verification', 'c'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'If you start writing an email in Gmail and close the tab before clicking Send, where is your unfinished message saved automatically?', 'Starred', 'Sent', 'Spam', 'Drafts', 'd'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'What is a "Browser Extension" (or Add-on)?', 'An extra long charging cable', 'A second monitor screen', 'A Wi-Fi booster antenna', 'A small optional helper tool added inside your browser (which you should install ONLY from trusted creators)', 'd'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'easy', 'If you want to save an online exam admit card or receipt neatly so you can view it offline anytime without internet, what can you select in the Print (`Ctrl + P`) destination menu?', 'Bluetooth Speaker', 'Save as PDF', 'Fax Machine', 'Delete Page', 'b'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'When a random flashy website suddenly asks "Allow this site to send you Notifications?", what is the smart habit if you do not need alerts from it?', 'Restart your router', 'Always click Allow on every site', 'Click "Block" — allowing shady sites to send notifications floods your screen with fake virus/ad pop-ups!', 'Enter your phone number', 'c'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'When sending an email announcement to 50 parents or students who do not know each other, why is `BCC` better than `CC`?', '`BCC` (Blind Carbon Copy) keeps everyone’s email address private from the other recipients', '`BCC` allows larger attachments', '`CC` deletes the email after reading', '`BCC` makes the email arrive faster', 'a'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'In an email thread sent to 40 club members, what happens if you click "Reply All" instead of "Reply"?', 'Your reply goes to ALL 40 people in the group instead of just the sender!', 'It replies only to yourself', 'It deletes all previous emails', 'It translates your message', 'a'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'Look closely at two URLs: `https://sbi.co.in` vs `https://sbi-login-kyc.freehost.xyz`. In the second URL, which company actually owns the real website domain?', 'State Bank of India', '`freehost.xyz` — the `sbi-login-kyc` part at the front is just a fake subdomain trick!', 'Google', 'Reserve Bank of India', 'b'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'If a webpage looks broken or keeps showing an outdated version even after refreshing, what browser step usually fixes it?', 'Uninstalling Microsoft Word', 'Lowering speaker volume', 'Hard Refresh (`Ctrl + F5`) or clearing cached images and files for that site', 'Replacing the mouse', 'c'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'In Chrome/Edge, why is creating separate "Browser Profiles" helpful when two siblings share one home laptop?', 'It makes Wi-Fi free', 'It creates two physical screens', 'It doubles the laptop hard disk size', 'Each sibling gets their own separate bookmarks, history, and logged-in school accounts without mixing them up', 'd'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'Why shouldn’t you blindly trust a shortened mystery link (like `bit.ly/3xYz99`) sent by an unknown stranger?', 'Short links only work on desktop PCs', 'Short links use 10 GB of data', 'Short links turn off Bluetooth', 'Shortened links hide the real destination website URL until clicked, so they can disguise phishing or scam sites', 'd'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'When sharing a Google Doc with a teammate, what is the difference between giving "Commenter" access vs "Editor" access?', 'An Editor cannot type anything', 'A Commenter can suggest notes without changing your original text; an Editor can directly change or delete content', 'A Commenter cannot even read the document', 'Both are identical', 'b'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'Why do most email services (like Gmail) stop direct attachments larger than 25 MB, and how do you send a 200 MB project video cleanly?', 'Videos can never be shared online', 'Cut the video into 200 separate 1-second emails', 'Email inboxes aren’t built for huge files — upload the video to Google Drive/OneDrive and share its link instead', 'Rename `.mp4` to `.txt` so it shrinks to zero', 'c'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'What does "Pinning a Tab" (Right-click tab → Pin) do in Chrome, Edge, or Firefox?', 'Shrinks the tab neatly to the far left without a close (✕) button so you don’t close it by accident', 'Sends the tab to your friends', 'Downloads every image on the page', 'Prints the tab on paper', 'a'),
  (12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'hard', 'When you hover your mouse over a button or link (without clicking yet), where does the browser preview the real destination URL?', 'In the bottom-left corner of the browser window', 'Behind the laptop screen', 'Inside the Recycle Bin', 'On the keyboard', 'a'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It pauses huge background Windows updates so your friend’s mobile data does not drain suddenly', 'It makes the screen brighter', 'It doubles keyboard speed', 'It uninstalls browsers', 'a'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', '`5G` Wi-Fi requires a 5G SIM card inside the router', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', 'There is no difference at all', '`2.4G` works only at 2:40 PM', 'b'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'What is "Quick Share / Nearby Share / AirDrop" on modern phones and laptops used for?', 'Deleting duplicate contacts', 'Scanning paper books', 'Sending photos or project files fast between two nearby devices wirelessly without wasting internet data', 'Charging another phone from 10 meters away', 'c'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'Why should you avoid logging into banking or sensitive accounts on an open, password-free public Wi-Fi at a railway station or café?', 'Public Wi-Fi deletes SIM contacts', 'Public Wi-Fi breaks your phone camera', 'Public Wi-Fi drains battery 10x faster', 'Unsecured open Wi-Fi networks make it easier for attackers nearby to snoop on traffic or set up fake twin hotspots', 'd'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'In online video calls or multiplayer games, what does "High Ping / High Latency" (e.g., 450 ms instead of 25 ms) feel like?', 'Extra crisp sound quality', 'Higher screen brightness', 'More storage space', 'A noticeable delay or lag between clicking/speaking and getting a response back', 'd'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'What brings ultrahigh-speed broadband into modern schools and homes using hair-thin strands of glass carrying pulses of light?', 'VGA Monitor Cable', 'Fiber-Optic Cable', 'Aux Audio Cable', 'Printer Ribbon', 'b'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'easy', 'If the home internet suddenly stops working on ALL phones and laptops at once, what safe 1-minute step often resolves a stuck router?', 'Cut the fiber cable', 'Factory-reset every phone in the house', 'Power-cycle the router: turn it OFF, wait 15–30 seconds, and turn it back ON', 'Reinstall Windows', 'c'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What does "NFC" (Near Field Communication) on modern phones and smart cards allow?', 'Tap-to-pay or instant pairing when held within a few centimeters of a reader/tag', 'Printing paper documents', 'Cooling the battery', 'Long-distance satellite TV reception', 'a'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'When you type `mapleskhatauli.com` in your browser, which behind-the-scenes internet phonebook translates that friendly name into the server’s numeric IP address?', 'DNS (Domain Name System)', 'UPS (Power Supply)', 'USB (Serial Bus)', 'PDF (Document Format)', 'a'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Your internet speed test shows `100 Mbps` (Megabits per second). Since 8 bits = 1 Byte, roughly how many Megabytes (`MB`) can download in 1 second?', 'Exactly 800 MB per second', 'Around 12.5 MB per second (`100 ÷ 8`)', '0.1 MB per second', '100 GB per second', 'b'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Why is setting up a separate "Guest Wi-Fi" network on a home or school router a smart security practice for visitors?', 'Guest Wi-Fi doubles your ISP plan speed', 'Guest Wi-Fi works 5 km away', 'Visitors get internet access while keeping your main school/home computers and shared printers isolated and private', 'Guest Wi-Fi needs no electricity', 'c'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What is "USB Tethering" between a smartphone and a desktop PC that has no Wi-Fi adapter?', 'Formatting the phone', 'Printing photos directly from SIM card', 'Tying the phone to the desk with a rope', 'Sharing your phone’s internet connection directly to the desktop PC through a normal USB charging/data cable!', 'd'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'What is the role of a "Firewall" in Windows or a school router?', 'It prevents physical fire in the computer room', 'It heats up the CPU in winter', 'It deletes old browser bookmarks', 'It monitors incoming and outgoing network traffic and blocks unauthorized outside connections', 'd'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Why should you change the default admin login (`admin / admin`) printed on the bottom sticker of a new home Wi-Fi router?', 'Default passwords use more electricity', 'Anyone connected nearby who knows common default logins could open router settings and change your Wi-Fi or DNS!', 'Otherwise Wi-Fi turns off after 24 hours', 'It voids the monitor warranty', 'b'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'When setting a Wi-Fi security type on a modern router, why should you pick `WPA2` or `WPA3` instead of `"Open"` or old `"WEP"`?', 'Security settings only change router LED color', '`Open` is the most secure setting', '`WPA2` / `WPA3` strongly encrypt your wireless Wi-Fi traffic, whereas Open/WEP are insecure', '`WPA3` blocks your own laptop from connecting', 'c'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'During a live Zoom/Google Meet class on weak internet, turning OFF your own HD video feed when not speaking helps audio stay clear because:', 'Live video uses much more bandwidth than voice, so pausing video leaves enough bandwidth for smooth audio', 'Microphones stop working when cameras are on', 'Audio does not use the internet', 'Webcams block the speakers physically', 'a'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What is the difference between a Modem (ONT) and a Wi-Fi Router (often combined into one box today)?', 'The Modem connects to the ISP’s outside fiber/cable line; the Router shares that internet across all your home devices', 'The Modem prints paper; the Router scans paper', 'The Router works without a Modem or ISP line', 'Modems are only for Bluetooth earbuds', 'a'),
  (12, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Where is the single best place in a house to keep a Wi-Fi router for even signal coverage across rooms?', 'Locked inside a thick steel almirah', 'In a central, open, slightly elevated spot — NOT hidden inside a closed metal cupboard or corner floor', 'Outside in the rain', 'Directly behind a microwave oven on the floor', 'b'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'To erase your photos', 'To slow down your internet', 'b'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'Change their account password', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'c'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Turn off spell check', 'Never read what you submit', 'Assume computers can never be wrong', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'd'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'Phones stop working after 10 PM', 'Night Wi-Fi costs double', 'Batteries charge only when silent', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'd'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Click every link they sent', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Send them your phone number to argue back', 'Keep it secret and worry alone', 'b'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Checking spelling in Word', 'Saving a backup copy on a pendrive', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'Using open-source software legally', 'c'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low', 'Twist sideways on one leg', 'Keep the monitor on the floor', 'Bend your neck 90 degrees inches from the keyboard', 'a'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '1930', '101', '108', '139', 'a'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'A high-resolution underwater nature video', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did', 'An encrypted ZIP file', 'A backup stored deep inside a folder', 'b'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Share bank OTPs on the call', 'Install a screen-sharing app they suggest', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!', 'Transfer money within 10 seconds in panic', 'c'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why do scammers urgently ask victims to install remote screen-sharing apps (like AnyDesk / TeamViewer / unknown `.apk`s) during fake "KYC / customer care" calls?', 'Banks require AnyDesk for every account', 'To double your mobile battery life', 'To clean dust from your phone speaker', 'Because screen-sharing lets the scammer see your live phone screen, including incoming bank OTPs and apps!', 'd'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'When designing a club registration form (Data Minimization principle), which information is ethical and sensible to collect?', 'Parents’ bank account numbers and Aadhaar passwords', 'Home Wi-Fi passwords of every student', 'Personal email passwords', 'Only what is genuinely needed for the club (Name, Roll No, Class, Section) — never unnecessary private family/financial data!', 'd'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What does a "Creative Commons (CC)" license on an online photo or music track tell students making a video project?', 'Nobody is allowed to view the image', 'The creator has given clear permission to reuse the work under stated conditions (such as giving proper attribution/credit)', 'The file contains a virus', 'You can sell it as your own painting without credit', 'b'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What should families do with old dead batteries, broken chargers, and discarded electronics ("E-Waste") instead of burning them or tossing them in open drains?', 'Break screens with a hammer in class', 'Burn plastic circuit boards in the backyard', 'Hand them over to authorized E-Waste collection/recycling centers so toxic metals don’t pollute soil and water', 'Throw batteries into rivers', 'c'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why do social media "recommendation algorithms" create an "Echo Chamber" if you are not mindful?', 'They keep showing more of whatever you clicked before, which can make one-sided opinions or rumors look like the whole truth', 'They delete posts older than 1 hour', 'They turn off Wi-Fi in closed rooms', 'They make your phone speaker echo loudly', 'a'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Before posting a close-up photo of your house keys, boarding pass barcode, or school exam admit card barcode publicly on Instagram/status, why should you pause?', 'Visible QR codes, barcodes, roll/application IDs, and personal details in photos can be scanned and misused by strangers!', 'Barcodes blur camera lenses', 'Social media bans white paper', 'There is no privacy risk at all', 'a'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is "Ransomware", and what single everyday habit best protects your school/home projects against it?', 'A free antivirus tool from Microsoft', 'Malware that locks files and demands money — keeping regular offline/cloud backups and avoiding shady downloads protects you!', 'A fast fiber router', 'A type of gaming keyboard', 'b'),
  (12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What does true "Accessibility" mean when students build a website or poster for the school community?', 'Making buttons 2 pixels small', 'Locking the site so nobody can open it', 'Using clear readable fonts, strong color contrast, and image descriptions (`alt` text) so everyone — including people with low vision — can use it comfortably', 'Using tiny light-yellow text on a white background', 'c');
